                            + "N11:curb-drop-probe N12:compass-fix "
                            + "N13:crossing/street-callouts+shoreline-earcon; "
                            + "iter-37-log: nav-beep nav-scan-stats nav-query nav-alert nav-hazard "
                            + "nav-guidance)");
                        driveLogger.Write("# vehicleaihandling: " + VehicleAIHandlingRegistry.LoadedFrom);
                        driveLogger.Write("# Started: " + DateTime.Now.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd HH:mm:ss"));
                        driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT iter-version: iter52-worlddata"); // iter-52 (WORLD DATA + FAILURE SNAPSHOTS — static world knowledge harvested from Rockstar's own decompiled scripts, plus the instrumentation to see a drive-assist failure instead of inferring it) // tools/build-worlddata.py harvests scripts/gta11y-worlddata.json from calamity-inc/GTA-V-Decompiled-Scripts@senpai: 50 letter scraps + 50 spaceship parts (case-dispatch Vector3 tables), 135 underwater cache pickups across 12 dive sites, 8 restricted-area groups as 56 angled boxes, 63 Strangers & Freaks trigger points (the func_118 table embedded in every re_*.c), 27 interactable props and the 33-entry random-event id registry. Parsed, not transcribed: hand-transcribing the RE ids got them wrong (re_securityvan is 9, not 8; id 8 is RE_BIKETHIEFSTAMP with no script). Read by WorldDataDb.cs on MapDb.Load's fail-closed contract // WORLD DIRECTORY (menu 9, collectibleNav + placesDirectory, both OFF): distance-sorted collectibles and places, waypoint + audio homing on the nav-assist emitter (880 Hz square, octave down when behind you, cadence by distance). Collected-state comes from GET_PACKED_STAT_BOOL_CODE, whose base index is not a literal anywhere — it is calibrated at runtime by matching a 50-bit popcount against STAT_GET_INT(num_hidden_packages_N) and FAILS CLOSED to showing everything, because telling someone they already found a collectible they have not is worse than a longer list. HAS_PICKUP_BEEN_COLLECTED is useless here: the scripts only CREATE_PICKUP within 50 m // RESTRICTED AREAS (restrictedAreaWarn, OFF): approach/enter/clear speech from the restrictedareas.c boxes, AABB-prefiltered so IS_POINT_IN_ANGLED_AREA is only paid for a candidate. Only 4 of 8 groups are named; the rest speak GET_NAME_OF_ZONE rather than a guessed landmark. Parameterised ceilings (IntToFloat(250 + iParam4)) are harvested as their base — writing null there would deserialize to 0 and collapse the box // INTERACTION CATALOGUE (interactionCatalogue, OFF): the ob_* scripts say what a prop is FOR, so the NumPad 8 scan appends it. Curated per script, not auto-scraped: the scrape returned 99 rows, mostly held props shared by the consumable scripts this mod already models properly // EVENTS AND SERVICES (menu 10): randomEventAlerts (OFF) reads Global_112911 and exposes SUPRESS_RANDOM_EVENT_THIS_FRAME; emergencyDispatch (OFF) is 911 without the phone UI via CREATE_INCIDENT services 7/5/3 from emergencycall.c, sited on a road node, DELETE_INCIDENT on timeout and onAborted. NO force-start: the brain system passes each re_ script its world point in ScriptParam_0.f_1 and START_NEW_SCRIPT cannot supply it, so 33 menu rows would all have reported "did not start" // FAILURE SNAPSHOTS: LogCollisionSnapshot had TWO call sites (AUTO-COLLISION, PLAYER-INDICATED-FAILURE) — every engine-stuck, stuck-layer, wedge-damage and damage-tally fired blind, which is why triage-log.py needs an unmarked-damage sweep. snapshotAllFailures (OFF) adds 13 tagged call sites, rate-limited per tag and while the car has not moved, reporting suppressedSinceLast. snapshotGeometry (OFF) appends a 16-way bumper fan + 8-way knee ring through CapsuleSweep (refused != clear), the entity table with relative bearings, chassis attitude and ground clearance. snapshotImage (OFF) writes JPEGs on a background thread and SELF-TESTS capture first — CopyFromScreen returns black under exclusive fullscreen, and a folder of black frames costs an analyst a session. snapshotPreroll (OFF) grows the snapshot ring 32->200 frames (~500 ms -> ~3.3 s; safe because every *LastMs query breaks on its time cutoff) and keeps 4 raw 1 Hz frames armed only on stuck signals, encoded only when a failure fires. triage-log.py copies them to triage/<stem>/snaps/ joined on collisionMarkerSeq and names them in digest.md; MARKER_RE now matches the SHAPE of a snapshot header (guarded by the preceding ==== rule) so a tag added in C# is picked up without a matching edit here // iter-51 (FOUR SYSTEMS against one session's evidence — on 08-11 the second steering channel steered the car BACKWARDS, a citywide riot recorded inCombat=0 on all 649 samples, every consume abandoned its animation at 95% with no outro, and the phone read ringtone names out as contacts) // DRIVE ASSIST — steerBiasV2 SIGN: SET_VEHICLE_STEER_BIAS is documented -1=full RIGHT / +1=full LEFT while control 59 in this mod is left-NEGATIVE, so the bias opposed lane-keep on every frame the gate was on; and because the native LOCKS steering rather than adding to it, that was lane-keep in reverse rather than a second opinion. Negated at its single write site; lastSteerBiasWritten now reaches the FRAME line (it was assigned and read by nothing, which is how the inversion survived a whole session); EVENT steer-bias carries cmd + bias + an honestly-named achSteerNormPrev // ONE steering denominator: commanded divided by min(0.61 rad, lockRad), achieved divided by the raw reported lock with no cap — so on TEZERACT (reported 19.0 deg, reached 40.1) an identical physical angle read 1.84x larger on the achieved side and pegged at its clamp. SteerNormLimitRad is now shared by both sides, and EffectiveSteerLockDeg believes the largest OBSERVED angle over a reported lock it exceeds by >10% (EVENT lock-override names the crossing; still bounded by the legacy 35 deg cap, so an observation can only widen the limit back toward the gate-off default, never past it) // roadSpeedGovernorV2 (OFF): a cap from the ENGINE's road class rather than the shipped graph — 2-lane 22 m/s, 4-lane 27, highway 33. The node-category governor reads pathNodeIndices and is inert on GPS-route paths, which is why 106 mph down a rural two-lane cost 1181 of the session's 1292 drawdown. Raises the shared speedzone request, so driver override and brake arbitration are unchanged (EVENT speed-governor) // polyDistrustV2 (OFF): roadFactsV2 measured the engine's road edge sitting a MEDIAN 6.0 m from the polyline being steered against (p95 33.1, max 79.7) — a parallel-road snap, and the mechanism behind the session's only player-marked failure. Past 4 m the cross-track term fades to zero while the heading term keeps full authority: heading hold, not hands off (EVENT poly-diverge). Both new gates consume roadFactsV2 and say so via EVENT gate-degraded when it is off // CIVIL UNREST — the scenario-ped density zeroing at stage 3+ is DELETED: it suppressed exactly the standing/sitting on-foot peds the recruiter recruits, at the moment the riot was supposed to escalate, and the roster tracked it one-for-one 3 -> 1 -> 0. Recruits are pulled OUT of their scenarios instead (normal exit below stage 3, panic above, then wander), roster cap 60 -> 64, and EVENT unrest-scan names every rejection reason beside the candidate count so an empty roster is finally attributable // INSTIGATORS, the narrow relaxation of the never-order-a-rioter rule: at most TWO tasked peds, armed, stage 2+, each on a DISTINCT hated target within 25 m, never each other, and no new orders while anything is still fighting. TASK_COMBAT_PED + SET_PED_KEEP_TASK + a temporary event block — which is what R*'s own re_gangfight.c does, and the direct rebuttal to hoping hate relationships start a fight unaided // heat decay 1.5/s -> 0.4/s (holding the stage-1 threshold used to require one fresh engagement every two seconds forever, so dynamic escalation was arithmetically unreachable and every advance read why=time), plus fires/alarms/dispatches as new inputs, plus unrestPace Relaxed/Normal/Fast because the ladder was a fixed ten minutes to citywide // POLICE: the incident anchor is the riot CENTROID and is recreated only on invalidity or a 60 m drift, not on a 60 s stopwatch that deleted a working dispatch and sent the units somewhere new — that churn IS the "going in circles". The COP -> faction hate edge is added at stage 3+ with police >= 2 (spoken, and torn down in both directions) so copsEngaged can leave 0; dispatched cops in stopped cars are asked to get out instead of being rejected for being in one; the copstop no longer early-returns past the scan that assigns copsEngaged; a roster that empties no longer publishes stale fighting/armed stats; unrest lines carry riotT= because driveLogFrameCount is frozen on foot and all 1663 of them read [F31198] // INTOXICATION — OUTROS: every consume ended by abandoning the enter clip at phase 0.95 and clearing tasks, so the bottle was never put down. The catalogue now carries per-intoxication-stage exit clips for the player AND the props, transcribed from the shared safehouse template (func_2 / func_6) and validated clip-by-clip against the game's own animation dictionary dump; a second synchronized scene plays them, and the audio-scene and bank teardown move after it (EVENT intox-exit) // kind=14's dictionary never existed — the real one has no trailing @ and holds only bartender and bottle clips, so it could never have been a solo consume; repointed at mp_player_intdrink, which is the actual solo bottle set with intro/loop/outro. Every clip is gated on GET_ANIM_DURATION > 0 (EVENT intox-clip-missing) so a bad name costs the outro instead of freezing the player. intoxDriveImpair and intoxBlackoutDrive finally have GateReach/GateFire call sites after censusing QUIET through the very session named after them // MENU READER — the phone page probe scored pages by "how many rows resolve" with no notion of which page belongs to the app that just opened, and chose the same page 4 at a perfect 16/16 for all four apps, which is why Contacts and Messages read out the ringtone and wallpaper list. It is now app-aware (a page whose signature is identical across two apps is a global table; a page where EVERY row resolves is a static one), refuses rather than guessing, and the working char-sheet contacts channel it had been shadowing runs first) // iter-50 (MENU READER v1.5 — the pause menu could NAME every settings row and say what almost none of them were SET to: 110 of 149 rows had no value source at all, whole panes of them, and pressing Left/Right was completely silent because the selection natives do not move on a value change, so the settings menu was navigable but not operable without sight) // A1 the pref -> profile-setting-id map is now LEARNED at runtime rather than hand-pinned: the profile store has been scanned since v1.1 and the reader has always known which row is highlighted, but nothing joined them — when exactly one id moves inside 900 ms of a Left/Right on a focused pref row, that id IS the row, and it is bound, spoken and persisted to gta11y-menubind.json so it survives the session (ambiguous multi-id moves are logged for tools/bind-profile-ids.py and bound to nothing, and a shipped pin always outranks a learned one) // A2 live value speech on Left/Right, plus the removal of the v1.4 mrRowLrCount suppression on the PROFILE path — that gate existed because the snapshot only committed on close, which stopped being true once the rescan follows the keypress; the settings.xml path KEEPS the suppression and says reader-value-nolive, because that file really is only rewritten when the menu closes // A3 position announcements (2 of 17) off the per-row ord, with the pane total taken from an observed paneRowCount when align-panes.py has one and a non-conditional row count otherwise, logged with its provenance so a wrong total is visible rather than merely wrong // A4 native value providers for the rows that are neither profile settings nor settings.xml keys — radio station and measurement system // A5 the open announcement is HELD 250 ms: 15 of 39 opens across the post-v1.4 sessions lived under a second (four of them one frame) before the frontend aborted and a second activation opened it for real, so one Esc press produced "Pause menu" / "Menu closed" / "Pause menu", and the middle utterance was a lie // B1 contact names were spoken as raw GXT KEYS ("CELL_FRANKLIN_N" 59 times across three sessions) because the char sheet stores a TEXT_LABEL and v1.4 returned it unlocalized; the rejection rules now live once in MenuLabelDb.ResolveGxt and an unresolved key is never spoken — "row 3" tells a blind user strictly more than an identifier does // B2 the contacts row map was the WRONG ARRAY: appcontacts.c line 9298 reads the selection through Global_21655 and v1.4 tried 21616 first behind a validator so weak (four entries, in-range and printable) that any array of small ints passed it, which is why rows 0 and 2 both resolved to slot 177 and the reader said the same contact twice on a monotone walk — candidates reordered, the validator now demands 6 distinct of 8, and an adjacent duplicate demotes the channel to "row N" // B3 phoneRowTextV2 (DEFAULT OFF): every phone app writes its visible rows into ONE shared array, Global_10324[char][page].f_7[row], as TEXT_LABELs handed to the scaleform by SET_DATA_SLOT — so a single provider reads Phone Settings, Checklist, Texts and Email instead of the per-app tables phoneAppRows was going to need, and the page index (the one unconfirmed offset) is probed and logged before anything is spoken // B4 the Texts/Email store sweep is RETIRED: it ran four sessions and only ever rediscovered the char sheet at base 2349, because those apps read their senders out of it — ~39k probes per app open for a base that is now pinned as data // B5 locked home tiles say so // iter-49 (THE ENGINE'S OWN ROAD MODEL — thirteen gates, ALL DEFAULT OFF, read out of the decompiled vanilla scripts rather than guessed, the same method that produced iter-44 through iter-48) — the lateral model, the junction detector and the stuck ladder were all built from shipped offline data (a paths.xml/junctions.xml dump, an 82-row JunctionDb, a hand-picked LANE_WIDTH_M) plus hand-tuned heuristics, while taxiservice.c and taxilauncher.c have contained a complete "find my lane / find the correct kerb / is this node driveable / am I stuck" implementation the whole time // A1 roadFactsV2 (TELEMETRY): GET_CLOSEST_ROAD gives live lanesFwd/lanesBwd/median-width plus the road edge as a real segment, and answers three questions open since iter-32 — do the shipped lane counts agree with the engine (BuildSteerPolyline bets the offset SIGN on them), is `width` the median gap the citizenfx contract says it is (which would confirm the iter-32 finding that paths.xml Width is not road width), and how far does our steering polyline sit from the engine's own edge (a DIRECT measurement of the parallel-arm snap iter-36 could only clamp); also picks up GET_NTH_CLOSEST_VEHICLE_NODE_ID + IS_VEHICLE_NODE_ID_VALID + GET_VEHICLE_NODE_IS_SWITCHED_OFF/IS_GPS_ALLOWED, the validation R* runs on every node and this mod ran on none, and the outLanes output all 14 node-query sites have allocated and discarded since iteration one // A2 nodePropsV2 (TELEMETRY): GET_VEHICLE_NODE_PROPERTIES returns eVehicleNodeProperties — OFF_ROAD ON_PLAYERS_ROAD NO_BIG_VEHICLES SWITCHED_OFF TUNNEL_OR_INTERIOR LEADS_TO_DEAD_END HIGHWAY JUNCTION TRAFFIC_LIGHT GIVE_WAY WATER — at any coordinate with nothing shipped, which is the whole of what the 82-junction database, the 1,443-node TrafficLight fallback and the street-name surface detector were approximating, plus give-way and dead-end which the mod had no concept of at all // A3 nodeQueryArgsV2: every node query in this file passed nodeFlags=1, which is not a default but GCNF_INCLUDE_SWITCHED_OFF_NODES — an explicit opt-IN to driveways, service spurs and disabled paths, and the likeliest mechanical source of the lat-snap the iter-36 clamp treats symptomatically; path sources now take IGNORE_SLIPLANES|IGNORE_SWITCHED_OFF_DEADENDS, the same-direction recovery search adds GCNF_FAVOUR_FACING (the engine doing in one call what FindNearestSameDirectionRoadNode does by iterating 1..10 and filtering a 45-degree window), recovery targets deliberately KEEP the switched-off nodes because a driveway is a fine place to be pushed back onto out of a ditch, nthClosest 0 -> 1 at the eleven sites passing an out-of-contract 0, and GET_APPROX_FLOOR_FOR_AREA as taxiservice's deck disambiguator in place of a flat 12 m Z window // A4 nodeHazardV2: consumes A2 — a THIRD junction arming source covering the whole map, arming LAST so a DB template still wins; a give-way governor and announcement; a dead-end warning plus a veto on recovering INTO one (driving out of a wedge into a cul-de-sac is how the 07-31 strand pattern starts); HIGHWAY lifting the coarse speed-category cap so a freeway is not governed to a surface-street speed; and TUNNEL_OR_INTERIOR vetoing the off-road arm, because under covered road IS_POINT_ON_ROAD reads False AND the polyline snaps to the street overhead, so BOTH halves of the "genuinely departed" conjunct fire at speed inside a tunnel. What this does NOT do is claim to know a light's COLOUR — IS_VEHICLE_STOPPED_AT_TRAFFIC_LIGHTS appears exactly once in the whole 1,156-script corpus and is widely reported unreliable, so a light still arms a slow-down governor and never a stop // B1 kerbGeometryV2 (TELEMETRY): taxilauncher.c's picker ported verbatim — both kerbs via GET_POSITION_BY_SIDE_OF_ROAD, the perpendicular of the near one dotted against the approach vector to choose the side reachable without crossing, +180 degrees on the heading if the far one was taken; the `side` parameter is UNDOCUMENTED so all three of R*'s values (0, 1, -1) are sampled and logged and the convention is settled from a session, exactly as the eMenuPref shift and the SteeringAngle sign were // B2 laneWidthV2: LANE_WIDTH_M is 5.3 m and R*'s own drop-off maths uses 4.2 m per lane, so the "half lane" bias has really been 2.65 m of a 4.2 m lane since iter-30 — most of a full lane, and on a narrow street the difference between the inside lane and the kerb; the one-way/two-way decision also moves off the shipped graph onto the live GET_CLOSEST_ROAD counts, and the latHalfW distrust clamp gets the same correction (a 4-lane road was credited 10.6 m of half-carriageway instead of 8.4 m, so blown lateral errors up to 2.2 m larger passed the test); deliberately NOT imported is taxiservice's full 4.2*lanes magnitude and its +0.9*width/-0.7 corrections, which walk a point to the KERB and belong to pullOverAssist // B3 pullOverAssist: a Pull Over command (Auto-Drive item 37) that stops at the kerb on the driver's own side — Full mode and AI drivers get a real park, Assistive mode gets a spoken bearing and a brake FLOOR any throttle press cancels, because seizing the wheel in Assistive would break the whole contract of the mode; the same kerb target replaces the raw road NODE in Park at Nearest Safe Spot and in the auto-drive park handoff, where the heading was veh.Heading — never a considered choice, simply wherever the nose happened to point when the handoff fired; targets are validated with IS_POINT_OBSCURED_BY_A_MISSION_ENTITY as taxiservice does // C1 engineStuckTelemetryV2 (TELEMETRY) + C2 engineStuckArmV2: IS_VEHICLE_STUCK_TIMER_UP has four types and the mod has read none of them for 48 iterations; taxiservice polls the fast pair at 7 s and the slow pair at 30 s, the type meanings are undocumented so all four are sampled at three thresholds beside upright/onAllWheels/roll (which is what will separate a roll detector from a jam detector) and beside the mod's own verdict; the arm is ADDITIVE ONLY and never a veto, because an engine timer that fails to fire must not be able to suppress an arm the heuristics got right — the rule the iter-43 queue-veto broke at a cost of a 32 s strand — and RESET_VEHICLE_STUCK_TIMER now runs on every release so a stale timer cannot re-arm instantly and produce a recovery loop that reads like a car which never got free // C3 tempActionV2: the most expensive bug in this project was the mod disabling the controls it was writing to, and even post-actuationV2 every rung of the recovery ladder still goes through that one channel; TASK_VEHICLE_TEMP_ACTION does not touch it at all, and vanilla uses it exactly where we use control writes (taxiservice holds a cab with TA_WAIT and stops it with TA_BRAKE_ACTION, re_bus_tours stops a coach the same way), so the pivot rungs get TA_HANDBRAKE_TURN_LEFT/RIGHT and the reverse rungs get TA_GO_IN_REVERSE instead of a ForwardSpeed velocity injection onto a car that may still be physically wedged; HARD-restricted to Full mode with a recovery already engaged, because a temp action is a task on the driver ped and takes the wheel from whoever holds it // C4 driveSequenceV2: taxiservice queues DRIVE_TO_COORD_LONGRANGE and TASK_VEHICLE_PARK as ONE OPEN_SEQUENCE_TASK and lets the engine own the handoff, against our hand-rolled Cruise->Navmesh->Park machine with its overshoot re-arm latch; the phase machine stays as the fallback and watches for an 8 s stall short of the destination, because the one thing the engine will not do is tell us it has given up, and a blind passenger sitting in a stopped car with no explanation is the failure this subsystem exists to prevent; TASK_VEHICLE_PARK also finally gets a real heading via DestinationParkHeading rather than the car's own // C5 steerBiasV2: SET_VEHICLE_STEER_BIAS is a steering write outside the control system (drunk.c swerves a car with it), staged as measurement first — write the bias, log it against the actuationFeedbackV2 achieved-angle readback, and promote it only if achSteer actually moves, because whether it does anything on a PLAYER-driven car is unverified // D gunfireAttribV2: iter-46 0b-4 established that 932.1 of 07-31's 1552.0 marked-damage units were police gunfire and that nothing in the log said so, leaving the analyst to infer it from wanted= — a poor proxy that is non-zero for whole minutes with no shots fired and zero during a gang shootout; taxiservice answers it directly with IS_BULLET_IN_AREA(7 m) and IS_PROJECTILE_IN_AREA(15 m), so bullet=/proj= now ride UNGATED on the marker header and the unmarked-damage sweep (measurement, iter-46 Stage 0b precedent) and triage grows a fire column plus a gunfire section, while the GATE covers only the behaviour: standing the damage-grind arm down under fire (its premise is "a stopped car losing health is being ground against something", which is exactly wrong when the health is coming off because someone is shooting) and a "Taking fire" cue // rollout: the four TELEMETRY gates change nothing perceptible and share one session; everything else is one gate per epoch per the iter-41 discipline // iter-48 (CIVIL UNREST ESCALATION OVERHAUL — the riot now escalates into the WORLD instead of only into combat attributes, because a stage-3 "full riot" differed from stage 1 by a few attributes and a slightly larger radius while traffic, ambience and police were untouched, which for a player who cannot see the riot meant the escalation the narration promised was never audible) — the mechanism designs come out of the decompiled vanilla scripts, not guesswork: joaat("COP")/joaat("ARMY") are real built-in relationship groups (re_arrests.c sets its criminal group Dislike toward COP with NO reverse edge, which is exactly the one-directional form used here), CREATE_INCIDENT(service,x,y,z,units,3f,&id,0,0) with a 60 s refresh is emergencycall.c's shape verbatim, vanilla's own ambient brawl (re_gangfight.c) runs CR_Near + 100 m perception for its MELEE variant and CR_Medium only for the gun variant which is why our stage 3 stood off, and PLAY_PED_AMBIENT_SPEECH_NATIVE's third argument is a speech PARAM not a voice name // 0 (UNGATED, lands first) RestoreUnrestPed leaked six things ApplyUnrestStageProfile/TryArmUnrestPed wrote — combat range, seeing 60 m, hearing 80 m, accuracy, attrs 27/49 and config flag 150 — so every ex-rioter inside the recruit radius stayed permanently hyper-alert after a riot ended, with no explanation a blind player could get; origAccuracy is now captured at recruit via GET_PED_ACCURACY and the orphan sweep mirrors the absolute resets it can know // 0b weapon-confiscation pass (BF_AlwaysEquipBestWeapon off + whitelist check on the profile slice), mandatory once police are in the fight because a rioter picking a Carbine Rifle off a dead cop silently breaks the "nothing automatic or long-range, ever" rule the weapon pools exist to enforce // 1 fifth stage "citywide riot" at 10:00 (0-3 keep their exact timings and names) + a heat model DARK-LAUNCHED behind unrestEscalation: heat rises on casualties/fresh engagements/player gunfire, decays 1.5/s of ModClock time, and is computed and logged every second while consuming nothing until the gate is flipped; stage selection is MONOTONIC by construction because a blind player told "full riot" must never then be told it calmed down while people are still fighting // 2 TickCivilUnrestFrame, a per-FRAME half — the population multipliers are _THIS_FRAME natives and TickCivilUnrest is gated to 4 Hz, so a density write inside that body would have been live for one frame in fifteen and done nothing observable; it also IS the teardown story, since _THIS_FRAME natives revert on the next frame after a crash whereas ADD_POP_MULTIPLIER_AREA's area id is process-local and unrecoverable // 3 unrestBrutality: CR_Near at stage>=3 is the single change that turns a standoff into a brawl, plus CanChaseTargetOnFoot / MaintainMinDistance off / SwitchToAdvanceIfCantFindCover / CanFlank / FrustratedAdvance / TLR_SearchForTarget / shoot rate 250-400 / move-rate override on the REGISTER slice because that native must be looped — and a deliberate safety INVERSION, blind fire from cover is turned OFF at brutality>=1 (BlindFireChance 0f) because "more brutal" must mean closer and more committed, not more unaimed rounds near someone who cannot see the shooter // 4 unrestAmbience: engine ped barks are the highest-value item here for a blind player (the crowd literally sounds like a riot at zero TTS cost) with pools chosen by VOICE COVERAGE so they actually fire on a random street ped, terrified bystanders mixed under shouting aggressors, and one-way arbitration where barks yield to the screen reader and never the reverse; car alarms 12-50 m; ped density 1.5-2.5x with scenario peds zeroed at stage>=3 // 4b unrestFires (double-gated, stage 4 only): 25 m hard floor, max 2, always announced Critical with a bearing at ANY verbosity, because a blind player who simply walks forward burns to death with no warning and FireIds are the one residual a hard reload cannot recover // 5 unrestTraffic on a roster entirely SEPARATE from unrestPeds (IsEligibleForUnrest still rejects anyone in a vehicle): aggressiveness/ability/wander speed by stage, driving styles built from the documented bit table and NOT from GetDrivingStyleFromFlags which reads the player's own Auto-Drive menu state; level 2 clears steers-around-peds and therefore HARD-REQUIRES Navigation Assist (its on-foot TTC alert is the only warning a blind pedestrian gets), clamping to level 1 and saying so when unmet, plus a 25 m no-arm bubble, a 10 m eject pass, and a 20% horn cue // 6 unrestPolice 0-4: level 1 is pure relationship work so "angry police" comes out of the same emergent mechanism as everything else, with a NEW wanted-level interlock because ReleaseUnrestCops only ever covered cops in the roster and level 1 recruits none — without it a player at 2 stars stands inside a rioter-versus-police firefight; level 2 delegates to the game's dispatch anchored 30-50 m OFF the player so sirens arrive nearby instead of converging onto them; level 3 is the ONE authorised order to a ped this mod does not own, a street stop whose outcome rolls arrest/taze/shoot at 80/15/5 -> 45/35/20 -> 20/40/40 by stage (lawful policing at stage 2, mostly beating and shooting people by stage 4), pistol forced for the shoot outcome so a carbine cop cannot spray and the line announced Critical at any verbosity; level 4 re-enables SWAT/army dispatch, whose spawn success at zero stars is UNVERIFIED and therefore logged as ok= rather than assumed // 6b SET_RIOT_MODE_ENABLED evaluated and REJECTED: its own documentation says all NPCs turn hostile including the player and it hands out uncontrolled pistols/SMGs, which breaks the group-level Respect invariant the feature is built on, bypasses the unrestMelee/unrestFirearms gates, and leaves the safety watchdog with nothing to eject from — vanilla director_mode.c never calls it either // 7 new EVENT kinds unrest-heat / unrest-traffic / unrest-driver / unrest-bark / unrest-police / unrest-copstop / unrest-firefight / unrest-alarm / unrest-fire / unrest-density / unrest-weapon-confiscate, and wanted= on unrest-combat as the specific evidence for the open question of whether config flag 42 covers crimes committed BY a flagged rioter against a cop // iter-47 (INTOXICATION PIPELINE, from the 2026-08-09 session where bank ok=1 + scene running + anim playing still produced no foley, and animations were cut off mid-move while the mod announced them finished) — all six root causes read out of the decompiled vanilla consumable scripts (ob_bong.c / ob_franklin_beer.c / drunk_controller.c), not guessed: A1 the consume was timed from the MENU PRESS against a hand-picked Consumable.Ms, so the anim dict's whole streaming window (up to 3 s) was billed to the animation and every safehouse clip was truncated — the clock now starts when the animation actually starts and its length comes from GET_ANIM_DURATION, with Ms demoted to a floor; A2 completion is now PHASE-driven off GET_SYNCHRONIZED_SCENE_PHASE >= 0.95 exactly as vanilla sequences these, with the wall clock kept only as a backstop, plus a scene-end path for a scene that stops on its own; A3 TASK_PLAY_ANIM duration Ms -> -1 (Ms told the engine to amputate the clip) with AF_LOOPING added only where the consume outlasts the clip; B1 START_AUDIO_SCENE was never called — an ambient bank makes the sounds RESIDENT and the audio scene is what ROUTES them, which is why loading the bank alone changed nothing; FRANKLIN/MICHAEL/TREVOR_SAFEHOUSE_ACTIVITIES_SCENE derived from the bank name and stopped on every exit path; B2 the synchronized scene now uses vanilla's blend 4f and flags 5 (USE_PHYSICS|DONT_INTERRUPT) instead of 8f/0 — DONT_INTERRUPT is what stops an ambient event nudging the player out partway through; B3 PLAY_SYNCHRONIZED_ENTITY_ANIM's BOOL return was discarded on both props, and the prop half is where the drink/smoke foley lives; B4 the scene no longer starts before the PROP MODELS are resident (08-09 logged prop2=0 on the first bong and prop2=1 on the two after it, and TickConsumeProp deliberately will not touch a prop the scene owns, so a late model was lost for the whole consume); C1 SET_GAMEPLAY_CAM_SHAKE_AMPLITUDE only scales a shake that is already running, so the drunk shake was dead after the one-shot expired — re-armed per frame the way drunk_controller.c does; C2 SET_AUDIO_SPECIAL_EFFECT_MODE moved off the raw hash cast, one-shot 0 on teardown; D1 EVENT intox-state heartbeat every 10 s carrying mode/clipset/impairment — intox-audio carried clipset= but fired on the one frame the clipset provably cannot be applied yet, so every log so far read clipset=none and the DrunkStage-from-clipset theory was untestable; D2 EVENT intox-done with why/ms/phase and ms= on the anim line, because on foot the frame counter never advances and [F0] was the only clock the log had; E1 re-selecting a consume now CANCELS it (1.5 s grace) — a synchronized scene blocks the sprint/movement interrupts, so a now-longer consume had no way out; E2 weapon forced to unarmed for the sequence as vanilla does, since a drawn weapon owns the same hand the prop attaches to; E3 whiskey second prop prop_cs_whiskey_bottle -> p_whiskey_bottle_s to match the model the clip was authored against; E4 vanilla-only mode no longer claims in a comment that the meters keep running six lines after zeroing them — it now speaks the end of the game's own drunk window instead of sobering up in silence // iter-46 Stage 0b+1 (MEASUREMENT + GATE INSTRUMENTATION, no behaviour change): 0b-1 collision-suppressed was an `else if` chained to the marker-SETTLE test, so every marker frame ALSO emitted a "discarded" event stamped reason=cooldown — 07-31 reported 1340.4 discarded against a real 10.4; 0b-2 the discarded total is now accumulated unthrottled (cumDrop=) and the line carries pos/street/lat/owner/mode/contact, which it never had; 0b-3 the steer actuation-divergence detector is speed-gated >3 m/s exactly as the brake detector was in iter-43 — the "43.1% of steer commands not actuated" headline was the same stationary-readback artifact for the third iteration running; 0b-4/0b-5 EVENT combat-state on every wanted transition + wanted= on every marker header, because 932.1 of 07-31's 1552.0 "marked damage" was police gunfire and nothing in the log said so; 0b-6 DEAD-VEHICLE/INTOX-STANDDOWN failClass + vehDead=/intoxSusp= on the header — a destroyed hull was classified UNKNOWN-STALE with assist=ON 14 s after it died // 1-1 GateReach/GateFire added to the 9 gates that had NONE (actuationV2, steerFreezeAtStop, reverseV2, brakeDeadzoneV2, graceArbitrationV2, recoverySuspendV2, recoveryTargetV2, stuckLadderV2, vehicleGeometryV2) — all of them censused eval:0/fire:0, which the digest rendered as "SILENT — never reached" and which was the reason no gate could be retired on evidence; 1-2 ONE EVENT gate-manifest driven by GATE_SETTINGS replaces five hand-written per-iteration emitters that had drifted (iter-44/45 never got one at all); 1-3 census carries dEval/dFire deltas so a gate that dies mid-session is visible on one line (junctionDirectionsV2 froze at fire:4048 for the last 44k frames and printed ACTIVE); 1-4/1-5 creepClearV2 and stuckArmHysteresisV2 counted their VETO as a fire, so the census read backwards — vetoes now counted separately; 1-6 offroadBrakeV2/roadModelV2 fires hoisted out of their log throttles so fire counts actions not log lines; 1-9 unit= per gate so eval:57453 (per frame) and eval:36 (per episode) are no longer compared as like quantities; 1-10 EVENT gate-quiet — a gate ON for 60 s with zero evaluations now says so // iter-43 (from the 266.7 MB / 53.2-driving-minute 07-31 field test) — A vehicleGeometryV2 (DEFAULT OFF): per-vehicle wheelbase in the pure-pursuit curvature feedforward (was a fixed 2.8 m "sedan"), per-vehicle steering-lock cap (was a fixed 0.61 rad), rear-overhang clamp 4.0->8.0 m in the reverse/bumper-true clearance checks, and mass+overhang-scaled BRAKE_DIST_*/MIN_BRAKE_DISTANCE; EVENT vehicle-geometry writes halfW/halfLen/mass/lockDeg/wheelbase per vehicle so vehicle SIZE is finally correlatable // B strand fix: queue-veto now expires after 8 s of a non-moving "queue" (EVENT queue-veto-expired), ACC standstill release is LATCHED against the ~1 Hz re-hold cycle, and immobile-under-throttle owns a spoken reason so a blind driver is never left flooring the pedal in silence (07-31: 32 s strand, 7 unanswered F1 flags) // C actuation telemetry corrections: SteeringAngle sign NEGATED (22,247 of 22,446 frames disagreed in sign; fit was -0.779*liveSteer) and the brake-divergence detector is speed-gated >3 m/s (BrakePower reads ~0 on a stopped car — the "52.9% dead brakes" headline was a readback artifact) // G junctionDirectionsV2: precondition relaxed to waypoint-OR-mission-tracking (GENERATE_DIRECTIONS_TO_COORD needs a coord, not a GPS route) + EVENT gen-dir-skip names which precondition rejected the sample + EVENT nav-state heartbeat // gates promoted to default ON on field evidence: creepClearV2 throttleAuthorityV2 skewGateV2 offroadBrakeV2 nodeStreamGuardV2 // iter-42 (game-metadata batch, ALL GATES DEFAULT OFF) — C1 nodeStreamGuardV2: ARE_NODES_LOADED_FOR_AREA guard on all 4 node-query sites, so a path-node streaming gap no longer reads as "off-road" nor collapses the polyline (EVENT nodes-not-loaded) // A1/A3 actuationFeedbackV2 + wheelStateV2: achieved-state readback (SteeringAngle normalised by HandlingData.SteeringLock, BrakePower, ThrottlePower) and per-wheel contact/slip/tyre + wheel-contact plane fit, conditional-emit to protect the log budget // A2: EVENT actuation-divergence, log-only detector for commanded-but-never-actuated brake/steer // B1/B2 roadBoundaryV2 + groundNormalV2 (DARK, feed nothing): measured carriageway via GET_ROAD_BOUNDARY_USING_HEADING and grade/camber via GET_GROUND_Z_AND_NORMAL_FOR_3D_COORD; curve-brake gravity term deferred until grade is cross-validated against the A3 wheel plane // C2/C3 junctionDirectionsV2: GENERATE_DIRECTIONS_TO_COORD as a map-wide junction backstop + cross-check (EVENT junction-disagree) and turn-by-turn speech // iter-41 Stage T (triage: rolling damage sweep, synthetic incidents, epoch comparison, marker-independent trend) + Stage 0 (observability: throttle-hold ledger across all 7 disable-71 sites, gate-census, gate-toggle/test-anchor, immobile-under-throttle, brake aPeak, rolling damage-tally, applied-throttle truth fix) + behaviour gates ALL DEFAULT OFF: creepClearV2, accStandstillV2, assistVoiceV2, throttleAuthorityV2, damageDrawdownV2, stuckArmHysteresisV2, offroadBrakeV2, skewGateV2, handbrakeBandV2 //  iter-40: reverseV2 (ForwardSpeed velocity-injection -> commanded reverse), brakeDeadzoneV2 (control-72 dead-zone pre-compensation + rate-scaled lane-depart cap + rolling-wheel handbrake gate), graceArbitrationV2 (watchdog latch order, brake-vs-throttle arbitration, governor spans grace), recoverySuspendV2 (hazard-aware handover + spoken direction + throttle hold + assist-suspend event), recoveryTargetV2 (blocked/receding target re-resolve, rear-slope sentinel, on-road pause timeout), stuckLadderV2 (roadway auto-reposition, pivot no-progress abort), roadModelV2 (poly-hold drift guard, softer gross-departure eject) // iter-39 Stage 0 (instrumentation) + Stage 1 (actuationV2: stop disabling the controls we write; scoped steer urgency; brake-demand caps; brake-episode measurement) + Stage 3 (watchdogV2: watchdog no longer cancels the recovery that armed it, post-release speed governor)
                        // W4.2: prove the fixes are present + their gate states in every log.
                        driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT pinfix-gates:"
                            + " damageSensor=alwaysOn"
                            + " shapeTestV2=" + getSetting("shapeTestV2")
                            + " accStandstillRelease=" + getSetting("accStandstillRelease")
                            + " steerFreezeAtStop=" + getSetting("steerFreezeAtStop")
                            + " distressFloor=" + getSetting("distressFloor")
                            + " actuationV2=" + getSetting("actuationV2")
                            + " watchdogV2=" + getSetting("watchdogV2")
                            + " brakePhysicsAssist=" + getSetting("brakePhysicsAssist"));
                        // iter-40: each group is independently revertible in-game, so a
                        // session's verdict is meaningless without knowing which were
                        // actually live. Emit the real setting values, never literals.
                        driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT iter40-gates:"
                            + " reverseV2=" + getSetting("reverseV2")
                            + " brakeDeadzoneV2=" + getSetting("brakeDeadzoneV2")
                            + " brakeDeadzone=" + BRAKE_CONTROL_DEADZONE.ToString("F2")
                            + " graceArbitrationV2=" + getSetting("graceArbitrationV2")
                            + " recoverySuspendV2=" + getSetting("recoverySuspendV2")
                            + " recoveryTargetV2=" + getSetting("recoveryTargetV2")
                            + " stuckLadderV2=" + getSetting("stuckLadderV2")
                            + " roadModelV2=" + getSetting("roadModelV2"));
                        // iter-46 1-2: the manifest supersedes the five hand-written
                        // per-iteration gates events (pinfix/iter40/41/42/43 above and
                        // below). It names every entry of GATE_SETTINGS, so it cannot
                        // fall behind the way iter41-gates did — that emitter still
                        // listed only the nine iter-41 gates two iterations later, and
                        // iter-44/45 never got an emitter at all. The legacy lines stay
                        // for ONE session so an older triage build still parses this
                        // log; delete them next iteration.
                        WriteGateManifest();
                        // iter-42: same one-gate-per-session discipline.
                        driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT iter42-gates:"
                            + " nodeStreamGuardV2=" + getSetting("nodeStreamGuardV2")
                            + " actuationFeedbackV2=" + getSetting("actuationFeedbackV2")
                            + " wheelStateV2=" + getSetting("wheelStateV2")
                            + " roadBoundaryV2=" + getSetting("roadBoundaryV2")
                            + " groundNormalV2=" + getSetting("groundNormalV2")
                            + " junctionDirectionsV2=" + getSetting("junctionDirectionsV2"));
                        // iter-43: same one-gate-per-session discipline.
                        driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT iter43-gates:"
                            + " vehicleGeometryV2=" + getSetting("vehicleGeometryV2"));
                        WriteTestAnchor("session-start");
                        driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT map-data:"
                            + " nodesV=" + NodeGraph.SchemaVersion
                            + " n=" + NodeGraph.NodeCount
                            + " streets=" + NodeGraph.StreetTableCount
                            + " streetNodes=" + NodeGraph.NodesWithStreet
                            + " extNodes=" + NodeGraph.NodesWithExtFlags
                            + " widthLinks=" + NodeGraph.LinksWithWidth
                            + " junctions=" + JunctionDb.JunctionCount
                            + " entrances=" + JunctionDb.EntranceCount
                            + " entrSnapped=" + JunctionDb.SnappedEntranceCount
                            + " nodesLoad=" + NodeGraph.LoadStatus
                            + " nodesFile=" + NodeGraph.LoadedFileInfo
                            + " juncLoad=" + JunctionDb.LoadStatus
                            + " juncFile=" + JunctionDb.LoadedFileInfo
                            + " mapLoad=" + MapDb.LoadStatus);
                        // iter-52: world-data census. Gated so a session that is not
                        // exercising any of it does not carry a line implying it was.
                        // The counts are what a triage read needs to tell "the feature
                        // found nothing" apart from "the feature had no data".
                        if (getSetting("worldDataDb") == 1)
                            driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT worlddata-load: "
                                + WorldDataDb.Census());
                        // iter-34 BS-3: one-shot accessor self-test on the first
                        // enriched nodes — proves GetStreetName/GetExtFlags/
                        // GetSpeedCategory reach real data, so an all-zero route
                        // later reads as "route has no attributes" (07-03: ext=0 on
                        // 100% of frames was genuinely the route), not "join dead".
                        if (NodeGraph.SchemaVersion >= 2)
                        {
                            int stNode = -1, exNode = -1, spNode = -1;
                            for (int i = 0; i < NodeGraph.NodeCount
                                && (stNode < 0 || exNode < 0 || spNode < 0); i++)
                            {
                                if (stNode < 0 && NodeGraph.GetStreetName(i).Length > 0) stNode = i;
                                if (exNode < 0 && NodeGraph.GetExtFlags(i) != 0) exNode = i;
                                if (spNode < 0 && NodeGraph.GetSpeedCategory(i) >= 0) spNode = i;
                            }
                            driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT v2-selftest:"
                                + " streetNode=" + stNode + "/"
                                + (stNode >= 0 ? NodeGraph.GetStreetName(stNode) : "-")
                                + " extNode=" + exNode + "/"
                                + (exNode >= 0 ? ((int)NodeGraph.GetExtFlags(exNode)).ToString("X") : "-")
                                + " spdNode=" + spNode + "/"
                                + (spNode >= 0 ? NodeGraph.GetSpeedCategory(spNode).ToString() : "-"));
                        }
                        // Iter-33: stale-data guard. The 07-02 session silently ran
                        // v1 node data (deploy without -IncludeData) with v2 feature
                        // gates on — flag that combination loudly, once.
                        bool anyV2Setting = getSetting("junctionAssist") == 1
                            || getSetting("wrongWayAlert") == 1
                            || getSetting("restrictionAwareWalk") == 1;
                        if (anyV2Setting && NodeGraph.SchemaVersion < 2)
                        {
                            driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT map-data-mismatch:"
                                + " schemaV=" + NodeGraph.SchemaVersion
                                + " junctionAssist=" + getSetting("junctionAssist")
                                + " wrongWayAlert=" + getSetting("wrongWayAlert")
                                + " restrictionAwareWalk=" + getSetting("restrictionAwareWalk")
                                + " hint=run-deploy.ps1--IncludeData");
                            Speech.Info("Map data outdated. Some assists inactive.");
                        }
                        // iter-35 L1: mirror every line actually spoken to the reader
                        // into the log. Without this the log records what the car did
                        // but not what the blind tester was told — the 07-03 audit
                        // could not distinguish a silent hold from an announced one.
                        Speech.LogSink = (txt, pri) =>
                        {
                            if (driveLogger != null && driveLogger.IsRunning)
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT speech:"
                                    + " pri=" + pri + " text=\"" + txt + "\"");
                        };
                        Speech.Info("Drive assist debug logging started");
                    }
                }
                else if (!driveLogEnabled && driveLogWasEnabled)
                {
                    Speech.LogSink = null;
                    driveLogger.Stop();
                    Speech.Info("Drive assist debug logging stopped");
                }
                driveLogWasEnabled = driveLogEnabled;

                // W2.1 (overhaul): stamp the damage signal EVERY tick, before the
                // debug-log block. Runs whether or not logging is on and whether or
                // not the assist scan ran this frame, so the escape ladder sees
                // damage even while the assist is suspended or asleep.
                UpdateDamageSensor(Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle()
                    ? Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle : null);

                // iter-43 A: the geometry helpers feed the STEERING and BRAKING
                // control law, so the handling cache must be warm whether or not
                // debug logging is running. SampleVehicleFeedback (below) is inside
                // the logging block and cannot be the only refresh point.
                RefreshHandlingCache(Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle()
                    ? Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle : null);

                if (driveLogger.IsRunning)
                {
                    Vehicle logVeh = Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle()
                        ? Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle : null;
                    // iter-42 A1/A3: sample achieved state BEFORE the frame line is
                    // built, and outside its thinning, so the values on a logged
                    // frame always belong to that frame.
                    SampleVehicleFeedback(logVeh);
                    if (logVeh != null || isAutodriving)
                        LogDriveAssistFrame(logVeh);

                    // Iter-9 Patch G: auto-collision detection. Compare chassis
                    // health frame-to-frame; a drop >= AUTO_COLLISION_HEALTH_DROP
                    // while the car is moving and on the ground is treated as a
                    // collision and emits the same snapshot shape as the F1
                    // player marker. The cooldown prevents multi-frame contact
                    // from flooding the log with duplicates.
                    // iter-30: was gated `&& !logVeh.IsInAir`, which silently DROPPED the
                    // worst crashes — airborne tumbles into terrain (iter-29 F1495 bodyDrop
                    // 111, F2506 bodyDrop 158 had NO marker) — and reset the health baseline
                    // so the first post-landing frame was skipped too. Run the delta compare
                    // regardless of air state; the speed>1.5 + damage thresholds below still
                    // reject noise. Air state is now just an `airborne=true` annotation.
                    if (logVeh != null)
                    {
                        float curH = logVeh.HealthFloat;
                        // iter-20 H6: HealthFloat alone is nearly blind to body
                        // impacts — the 224937 session accumulated 42 pts of
                        // BodyHealth damage (incl. the flagged pier collision)
                        // with ZERO AUTO-COLLISION events. Track body + engine
                        // alongside, fire on any of the three dropping, and
                        // lower the speed gate 3 -> 1.5 m/s so pier-class
                        // low-speed hits register.
                        float curBody = logVeh.BodyHealth;
                        float curEngine = logVeh.EngineHealth;
                        bool sameVeh = logVeh.Handle == autoCollisionLastVehHandle;
                        // iter-35 L6: always-on teleport trace (trainer warps included).
                        // iter-39 L8: the handle gate used to be == (same vehicle only),
                        // which skipped a teleport that came WITH a vehicle change by
                        // construction — precisely the 07-23 case. Compare position
                        // only; record whether the vehicle also changed.
                        if (logTelePrevPos != GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero)
                        {
                            float tdx = logVeh.Position.X - logTelePrevPos.X;
                            float tdy = logVeh.Position.Y - logTelePrevPos.Y;
                            float tPlanar = (float)Math.Sqrt(tdx * tdx + tdy * tdy);
                            if (tPlanar > LOG_TELEPORT_JUMP_M)
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT teleport:"
                                    + " from=" + FmtV(logTelePrevPos)
                                    + " to=" + FmtV(logVeh.Position)
                                    + " dist=" + tPlanar.ToString("F0")
                                    + " vehChanged=" + (logTelePrevVehHandle != logVeh.Handle));
                        }
                        logTelePrevPos = logVeh.Position;
                        logTelePrevVehHandle = logVeh.Handle;

                        // iter-39 L8: vehicle-session boundary. Fires on ANY change of
                        // the driven vehicle, including one separated by an on-foot
                        // stretch, so per-vehicle health accounting is possible.
                        if (logVeh.Handle != vehSessionHandle)
                        {
                            if (vehSessionHandle != 0)
                            {
                                float sdx = logVeh.Position.X - vehSessionPos.X;
                                float sdy = logVeh.Position.Y - vehSessionPos.Y;
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT vehicle-session:"
                                    + " kind=change oldHandle=" + vehSessionHandle
                                    + " oldModel=" + vehSessionModel
                                    + " oldBh=" + vehSessionBh.ToString("F0")
                                    + " oldEh=" + vehSessionEh.ToString("F0")
                                    + " newHandle=" + logVeh.Handle
                                    + " newModel=" + (logVeh.DisplayName ?? "-").Replace(" ", "")
                                    + " newBh=" + curBody.ToString("F0")
                                    + " newEh=" + curEngine.ToString("F0")
                                    + " gapMs=" + (vehSessionLastTicks > 0
                                        ? ((ModClock.Ticks - vehSessionLastTicks) / 10000L) : -1L)
                                    + " jumpM=" + ((float)Math.Sqrt(sdx * sdx + sdy * sdy)).ToString("F0")
                                    + " from=" + FmtV(vehSessionPos)
                                    + " to=" + FmtV(logVeh.Position));
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT vehicle-session:"
                                    + " kind=first handle=" + logVeh.Handle
                                    + " model=" + (logVeh.DisplayName ?? "-").Replace(" ", "")
                                    + " bh=" + curBody.ToString("F0")
                                    + " eh=" + curEngine.ToString("F0")
                                    + " pos=" + FmtV(logVeh.Position));
                            }
                            // ---- iter-43 A5: WRITE THE GEOMETRY DOWN ----
                            // The mod measures true model extents, steering lock and
                            // mass for every vehicle and logged NONE of it, which is
                            // why "are trucks worse?" could not be answered from a
                            // 266.7 MB / 19-vehicle session — the epoch table had no
                            // size column to correlate against. One line per vehicle,
                            // so this costs nothing per frame.
                            RefreshHandlingCache(logVeh);
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 vgHalf;
                            try { vgHalf = GetVehicleHalfDims(logVeh); }
                            catch { vgHalf = GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero; }
                            driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT vehicle-geometry:"
                                + " model=" + (logVeh.DisplayName ?? "-").Replace(" ", "")
                                + " halfW=" + vgHalf.X.ToString("F2")
                                + " halfLen=" + vgHalf.Y.ToString("F2")
                                + " halfH=" + vgHalf.Z.ToString("F2")
                                + " mass=" + handlingMass.ToString("F0")
                                + " lockDeg=" + handlingSteerLockDeg.ToString("F1")
                                // iter-51: the denominator the steering law will
                                // actually divide by for this vehicle, printed once
                                // at vehicle change so the whole session's steer
                                // numbers have a stated scale.
                                + " limitDeg=" + (SteerNormLimitRad(geometryV2Cached) * 180f / (float)Math.PI).ToString("F1")
                                + " wheelbase=" + GetVehicleWheelbase(logVeh).ToString("F2")
                                + " brakeScale=" + VehicleBrakeScale(logVeh).ToString("F2")
                                + " gate=" + getSetting("vehicleGeometryV2")
                                + " class=" + logVeh.ClassType);
                            // iter-46 1-1: fire = the per-vehicle geometry was actually
                            // resolved and published for a vehicle (once per vehicle),
                            // as distinct from reach, which counts consumer calls.
                            if (getSetting("vehicleGeometryV2") == 1)
                                GateFire("vehicleGeometryV2");
                            vehSessionHandle = logVeh.Handle;
                            vehSessionModel = (logVeh.DisplayName ?? "-").Replace(" ", "");
                        }
                        vehSessionBh = curBody;
                        vehSessionEh = curEngine;
                        vehSessionPos = logVeh.Position;
                        vehSessionLastTicks = ModClock.Ticks;
                        if (sameVeh && autoCollisionLastHealth > 0f)
                        {
                            float drop = autoCollisionLastHealth - curH;
                            float bodyDrop = autoCollisionLastBodyHealth > 0f
                                ? autoCollisionLastBodyHealth - curBody : 0f;
                            float engineDrop = autoCollisionLastEngineHealth > 0f
                                ? autoCollisionLastEngineHealth - curEngine : 0f;
                            // iter-28 P1 / W2.1: the lastBodyDropTicks/firstBodyDropTicks
                            // stamps moved to the always-on UpdateDamageSensor (called
                            // above, before this logger-gated block) so damage-armed
                            // recovery works with logging off. This block keeps only its
                            // diagnostic EVENT logging below.
                            long geNow = ModClock.Ticks; // pause-proof: grind-episode + collision-debounce durations (a pause must not look like a grind gap or fresh damage)
                            // iter-34 BS-1: a jump UP this big on the same handle is a
                            // replaced/repaired vehicle (GTA reuses handles) — log the
                            // swap and skip delta math this frame (baselines update below).
                            if (autoCollisionLastBodyHealth > 0f
                                && curBody - autoCollisionLastBodyHealth >= VEHICLE_SWAP_HEALTH_JUMP)
                            {
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT vehicle-swap:"
                                    + " kind=health-jump oldBh=" + autoCollisionLastBodyHealth.ToString("F0")
                                    + " newBh=" + curBody.ToString("F0")
                                    + " handle=" + logVeh.Handle
                                    + " model=" + logVeh.DisplayName);
                                grindEpisodeStartTicks = 0;
                                // firstBodyDropTicks reset now owned by UpdateDamageSensor (W2.1)
                                bodyDrop = 0f; engineDrop = 0f; drop = 0f;
                            }
                            // iter-35 L4: trainer REPAIRS jump health up by less than the
                            // swap threshold and were invisible (07-03: 979->1000 and
                            // 992->1000 fired nothing), silently corrupting damage
                            // accounting. Health never rises on its own, so any upward
                            // step >=5 is an external repair.
                            else if ((autoCollisionLastBodyHealth > 0f
                                        && curBody - autoCollisionLastBodyHealth >= 5f)
                                     || (autoCollisionLastEngineHealth > 0f
                                        && curEngine - autoCollisionLastEngineHealth >= 5f))
                            {
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT vehicle-repair:"
                                    + " dBh=" + (curBody - autoCollisionLastBodyHealth).ToString("F0")
                                    + " dEh=" + (curEngine - autoCollisionLastEngineHealth).ToString("F0")
                                    + " newBh=" + curBody.ToString("F0")
                                    + " newEh=" + curEngine.ToString("F0")
                                    + " full=" + (curBody >= 999f && curEngine >= 999f));
                                grindEpisodeStartTicks = 0;
                                // firstBodyDropTicks reset now owned by UpdateDamageSensor (W2.1)
                                bodyDrop = 0f; engineDrop = 0f; drop = 0f;
                            }
                            // iter-34 BS-1: DEATH CLIFF — a one-frame collapse to a dead
                            // hull is a vehicle DEATH, not a grind (07-03 marker #4
                            // logged bh 810->0 as kind=grind -809.7). A dead wreck's
                            // decaying health must not feed markers either.
                            bool vehDeadNow = curBody <= 0f && curEngine <= 0f;
                            bool deathCliff = bodyDrop >= DEATH_CLIFF_BODY_DROP
                                && (curBody <= 0f || curEngine < 0f);
                            if (deathCliff)
                            {
                                long geStartAtDeath = grindEpisodeStartTicks; // iter-36 P0-3: grind-end zeroes it below
                                if (grindEpisodeStartTicks != 0)
                                {
                                    driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT grind-end:"
                                        + " reason=death durMs=" + ((geNow - grindEpisodeStartTicks) / 10000)
                                        + " cumBhDrop=" + (grindEpisodeStartBh - curBody).ToString("F1")
                                        + " cumEhDrop=" + (grindEpisodeStartEh - curEngine).ToString("F1")
                                        + " contact=" + grindEpisodeContact);
                                    grindEpisodeStartTicks = 0;
                                }
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT vehicle-death:"
                                    + " bodyDrop=" + bodyDrop.ToString("F1")
                                    + " engineDrop=" + engineDrop.ToString("F1")
                                    + " bh=" + curBody.ToString("F0")
                                    + " eh=" + curEngine.ToString("F0")
                                    + " spd=" + logVeh.Speed.ToString("F1")
                                    + " pos=(" + logVeh.Position.X.ToString("F1") + ","
                                    + logVeh.Position.Y.ToString("F1") + ")"
                                    // iter-36 P0-3: link the death to its causal chain —
                                    // iter-35's two deaths needed a hand-join across three
                                    // artifacts to find mode/layer/attacker.
                                    + " mode=" + currentDriveMode
                                    + " layer=" + stuckLayer
                                    + " rev=" + alignmentEngageReverse
                                    + " lastMarker=" + collisionMarkerSeq
                                    + " sinceGrindStartMs=" + (geStartAtDeath != 0
                                        ? (geNow - geStartAtDeath) / 10000 : -1)
                                    + " sinceFirstDamageMs=" + (firstBodyDropTicks != 0
                                        ? (DateTime.Now.Ticks - firstBodyDropTicks) / 10000 : -1) // firstBodyDropTicks is wall-stamped elsewhere — keep clocks matched
                                    + " attacker=" + IdentifyAttacker(logVeh));
                                autoCollisionLastTicks = geNow;
                            }
                            // iter-34 BS-2: grind-episode state machine — one episode
                            // with duration + cumulative damage + contact entity,
                            // complementing the per-hit markers below.
                            bool grindDamage = (bodyDrop >= 2f || engineDrop >= 2f)
                                && logVeh.Speed < GRIND_EPISODE_MAX_SPEED
                                && curBody > 0f && !deathCliff;
                            if (grindDamage)
                            {
                                if (grindEpisodeStartTicks == 0)
                                {
                                    grindEpisodeStartTicks = geNow;
                                    grindEpisodeStartFrame = driveLogFrameCount;
                                    grindEpisodeStartBh = autoCollisionLastBodyHealth;
                                    grindEpisodeStartEh = autoCollisionLastEngineHealth;
                                    grindEpisodeContact = NearestContactLabel();
                                    driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT grind-start:"
                                        + " bh0=" + grindEpisodeStartBh.ToString("F0")
                                        + " eh0=" + grindEpisodeStartEh.ToString("F0")
                                        + " contact=" + grindEpisodeContact
                                        + " lat=" + lastLaneLateralError.ToString("F1")
                                        + " spd=" + logVeh.Speed.ToString("F1")
                                        + " mode=" + currentDriveMode
                                        + " rev=" + alignmentEngageReverse);
                                }
                                grindEpisodeLastDamageTicks = geNow;
                                string geContact = NearestContactLabel();
                                if (geContact != "none") grindEpisodeContact = geContact;
                            }
                            else if (grindEpisodeStartTicks != 0
                                && geNow - grindEpisodeLastDamageTicks > GRIND_EPISODE_END_TICKS)
                            {
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT grind-end:"
                                    + " durMs=" + ((geNow - grindEpisodeStartTicks) / 10000)
                                    + " frames=" + (driveLogFrameCount - grindEpisodeStartFrame)
                                    + " cumBhDrop=" + (grindEpisodeStartBh - curBody).ToString("F1")
                                    + " cumEhDrop=" + (grindEpisodeStartEh - curEngine).ToString("F1")
                                    + " contact=" + grindEpisodeContact);
                                grindEpisodeStartTicks = 0;
                            }
                            long sinceLast = ModClock.Ticks - autoCollisionLastTicks; // ModClock pair (written from geNow / below)
                            // iter-39 L2: feed an open settling window BEFORE this
                            // frame can open a new one, so the trigger frame is
                            // counted exactly once (the marker branch seeds the
                            // window with its own drop).
                            if (markerSettleStartTicks != 0)
                            {
                                markerSettleBh += bodyDrop;
                                markerSettleEh += engineDrop;
                                if (logVeh.Speed > markerSettlePeakSpd) markerSettlePeakSpd = logVeh.Speed;
                                if (bodyDrop > 0f || engineDrop > 0f) markerSettleDamagedFrames++;
                            }
                            bool fastImpact = !deathCliff && !vehDeadNow
                                && (drop >= AUTO_COLLISION_HEALTH_DROP
                                    || bodyDrop >= AUTO_COLLISION_BODY_DROP
                                    || engineDrop >= AUTO_COLLISION_BODY_DROP)
                                && logVeh.Speed > 1.5f;
                            // iter-25 M5: LOW-SPEED GRIND. A wedged car grinding props at
                            // <1.5 m/s took -68 bh / -31 eh in 06-18 (F6074-F6830) with
                            // ZERO AUTO-COLLISION — the >1.5 m/s gate missed all of it.
                            // Catch body/engine drops at crawl/stop too (slightly larger
                            // threshold to skip curb-scrape noise), labelled kind=grind.
                            bool grindImpact = !fastImpact && !deathCliff && !vehDeadNow
                                && logVeh.Speed <= GRIND_EPISODE_MAX_SPEED
                                && (bodyDrop >= GRIND_BODY_DROP || engineDrop >= GRIND_BODY_DROP);
                            // iter-39 L5: THE MARKER HOLE. fastImpact needs >= 8 and
                            // grindImpact used to need <= 1.5 m/s, so a 5-8 drop at
                            // speed produced NO marker at all. 07-23 F11304 lost 6.2
                            // body at 16.3 m/s and then rolled a 5 s / 10.7-body wall
                            // scrape (damage-tally F11319) with zero failure marker.
                            // Any drop >= GRIND_BODY_DROP now marks, at any speed;
                            // the kind= label just records which band it came from.
                            bool scrapeImpact = !fastImpact && !grindImpact && !deathCliff && !vehDeadNow
                                && logVeh.Speed > GRIND_EPISODE_MAX_SPEED
                                && (bodyDrop >= GRIND_BODY_DROP || engineDrop >= GRIND_BODY_DROP);
                            // iter-46 0b-1: hoisted so the suppressed branch below can
                            // exclude a frame that MARKED. See the else-if fix there.
                            bool markedThisFrame = (fastImpact || grindImpact || scrapeImpact)
                                && sinceLast > AUTO_COLLISION_COOLDOWN_TICKS;
                            if (markedThisFrame)
                            {
                                LogCollisionSnapshot("AUTO-COLLISION",
                                    (grindImpact ? "kind=grind " : scrapeImpact ? "kind=scrape " : "")
                                    + "healthDelta=-" + drop.ToString("F1")
                                    + " bodyDelta=-" + bodyDrop.ToString("F1")
                                    + " engineDelta=-" + engineDrop.ToString("F1")
                                    + " impactSpeed=" + logVeh.Speed.ToString("F1")
                                    + " attacker=" + IdentifyAttacker(logVeh) // iter-36 P0
                                    + (logVeh.IsInAir ? " airborne=true" : "")); // iter-28 L / iter-30 air
                                autoCollisionLastTicks = ModClock.Ticks;
                                // iter-39 L2: open a settling window. The marker header
                                // can only ever carry ONE FRAME of damage, but a real
                                // impact keeps accruing for ~1 s — and the cooldown
                                // right below deliberately suppresses those follow-up
                                // frames, so the number on the marker is the SMALLEST
                                // one. 07-23 markers #7 and #8 read healthDelta=-0.0
                                // while actually costing 163.5/349.9 and 83.7/177.9.
                                // Everything downstream (failure table, log-index
                                // worstDelta/totalDelta, the cross-session trend) was
                                // built on that first-frame value.
                                markerSettleSeq = collisionMarkerSeq;
                                markerSettleStartTicks = geNow;
                                markerSettleStartFrame = driveLogFrameCount;
                                markerSettleBh = bodyDrop;
                                markerSettleEh = engineDrop;
                                markerSettlePeakSpd = logVeh.Speed;
                                markerSettleDamagedFrames = 0;
                            }
                            // iter-39 L2: close the window and publish the REAL cost of
                            // the marker. triage reads this and overrides the header's
                            // first-frame healthDelta with it.
                            if (markerSettleStartTicks != 0
                                && geNow - markerSettleStartTicks > AUTO_COLLISION_COOLDOWN_TICKS)
                            {
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT marker-settle:"
                                    + " marker=" + markerSettleSeq
                                    + " winMs=" + ((geNow - markerSettleStartTicks) / 10000)
                                    + " bhDrop=" + markerSettleBh.ToString("F1")
                                    + " ehDrop=" + markerSettleEh.ToString("F1")
                                    + " frames=" + (driveLogFrameCount - markerSettleStartFrame)
                                    + " damagedFrames=" + markerSettleDamagedFrames
                                    + " peakSpd=" + markerSettlePeakSpd.ToString("F1")
                                    + " contact=" + NearestContactLabel());
                                markerSettleStartTicks = 0;
                            }
                            // iter-30: a real drop rejected by cooldown (a second hit in a
                            // multi-impact crash) or by the damage threshold used to vanish.
                            // Leave a lightweight trace + running count so the next analysis
                            // can tell a deduped/thresholded impact from a clean stretch.
                            //
                            // iter-46 0b-1: this was an `else if` CHAINED TO THE MARKER-SETTLE
                            // `if` ABOVE, not to the marker `if`. On the frame a marker fires,
                            // markerSettleStartTicks is set to geNow, so `geNow - start` is 0,
                            // the settle test is false, and control fell straight into here —
                            // emitting a "discarded" event for damage that had just been
                            // MARKED, stamped reason=cooldown (true only because the marker
                            // fired). 07-31 printed 25 such rows totalling 854.1, and the
                            // digest's "discarded damage" was 1340.4 against a real 10.4.
                            // Now an independent `if`, explicitly excluding a marked frame.
                            //
                            // iter-46 0b-2: the running total is accumulated UNTHROTTLED. The
                            // 500 ms log throttle stays on the LINE (it is what keeps a
                            // multi-impact crash from flooding the log), but it used to gate
                            // the counter too, so "discarded total" was a floor set by a log
                            // throttle rather than a measurement.
                            bool suppressedDrop = !markedThisFrame
                                && (bodyDrop >= 2f || engineDrop >= 2f || drop >= 2f)
                                && !deathCliff && !vehDeadNow; // iter-34 BS-1: wreck decay is not a suppressed hit
                            if (suppressedDrop)
                            {
                                suppressedCollisionCount++;
                                suppressedCollisionDropCum += bodyDrop + engineDrop;
                            }
                            if (suppressedDrop
                                && driveLogger != null && driveLogger.IsRunning
                                && DateTime.Now.Ticks - lastCollisionSuppressLogTicks > 5000000)
                            {
                                lastCollisionSuppressLogTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;
                                driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT collision-suppressed:"
                                    // iter-33: "speed-gate" = grind-magnitude drop but too fast
                                    // for the grind detector and too small for fastImpact — the
                                    // gap between the two gates, previously lumped in below-threshold.
                                    // iter-46 0b-1: "cooldown" no longer overlaps a marked
                                    // frame (those never reach here now), so it means what it
                                    // says: a genuine second hit inside the 1 s window.
                                    + " reason=" + ((fastImpact || grindImpact) ? "cooldown"
                                        : (logVeh.Speed > 1.5f
                                           && (bodyDrop >= GRIND_BODY_DROP || engineDrop >= GRIND_BODY_DROP))
                                            ? "speed-gate" : "below-threshold")
                                    + " bodyDelta=-" + bodyDrop.ToString("F1")
                                    + " engineDelta=-" + engineDrop.ToString("F1")
                                    + " healthDelta=-" + drop.ToString("F1")
                                    + " spd=" + logVeh.Speed.ToString("F1")
                                    + (logVeh.IsInAir ? " airborne=true" : "")
                                    + " sinceLastMs=" + (sinceLast / 10000L)
                                    + " total=" + suppressedCollisionCount
                                    // iter-46 0b-2: the unthrottled running total, so the
                                    // digest can report real discarded damage instead of the
                                    // sum of whatever lines survived the 500 ms throttle.
                                    + " cumDrop=" + suppressedCollisionDropCum.ToString("F1")
                                    // iter-46 0b-2: this channel carried the ONLY trace of
                                    // real damage on 07-31 and had no position, street, lane
                                    // offset, brake owner, mode or contact — the digest's
                                    // contact column was "-" for all 25 rows. Bounded at
                                    // <=2 lines/s by the throttle above, so the byte cost is
                                    // negligible.
                                    + " pos=" + FmtV(logVeh.Position)
                                    + " street=" + World.GetStreetName(logVeh.Position)
                                    + " lat=" + lastLaneLateralError.ToString("F2")
                                    + " owner=" + BrakeOwnerName()
                                    + " mode=" + currentDriveMode
                                    + " contact=" + NearestContactLabel());
                                SnapshotFailure("COLLISION-SUPPRESSED", null);
                            }
                            // iter-36 P1-5: DAMAGE TALLY. Per-frame drops < 2 never
                            // reach any detector above; 5 s of them is real scrape
                            // damage with zero trace (F29422-class episodes). Roll a
                            // 5 s window of ALL drops; if >= 5 total landed with no
                            // marker/grind coverage in the window, leave a tally.
                            // iter-41 Stage 0.13: the window used to TUMBLE — on
                            // expiry the accumulators were zeroed and a fresh window
                            // began, so an episode straddling the boundary was split
                            // and each half tested against the >=5 floor separately.
                            // On 07-28 that reported the session's largest damage
                            // event as 10.5 when it was really 15.0: the 4.5 remainder
                            // started the next window and never reached the floor.
                            // Carry the remainder forward instead of discarding it.
                            if (bodyDrop > 0f) { dmgTallyBh += bodyDrop; dmgTallyLastDropTicks = geNow; }
                            if (engineDrop > 0f) { dmgTallyEh += engineDrop; dmgTallyLastDropTicks = geNow; }
                            if (dmgTallyWindowStartTicks == 0)
                                dmgTallyWindowStartTicks = geNow;
                            else if (geNow - dmgTallyWindowStartTicks > 50000000L
                                     // Hold the window open while damage is still
                                     // arriving; close it 1.5 s after the last drop so
                                     // one physical episode reports as one number.
                                     && (dmgTallyLastDropTicks == 0
                                         || geNow - dmgTallyLastDropTicks > 15000000L))
                            {
                                bool tallyCovered =
                                    (geNow - autoCollisionLastTicks) < 50000000L
                                    || grindEpisodeStartTicks != 0
                                    || deathCliff || vehDeadNow;
                                if (!tallyCovered && dmgTallyBh + dmgTallyEh >= 5f)
                                    driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT damage-tally:"
                                        + " winMs=" + ((geNow - dmgTallyWindowStartTicks) / 10000)
                                        + " bhDrop=" + dmgTallyBh.ToString("F1")
                                        + " ehDrop=" + dmgTallyEh.ToString("F1")
                                        + " spd=" + logVeh.Speed.ToString("F1")
                                        + " contact=" + NearestContactLabel()
                                        // iter-49 D (UNGATED): the unmarked-damage sweep is
                                        // where gunfire hides — it fires precisely when no
                                        // collision was detected, which is what being shot at
                                        // looks like. Without these two the digest counts it
                                        // as unexplained driving damage.
                                        + " bullet=" + underFireNow
                                        + " proj=" + projectileNear
                                        + " wanted=" + Game.Player.WantedLevel
                                        + " pos=" + FmtV(logVeh.Position));
                                    SnapshotFailure("DAMAGE", null);
                                dmgTallyWindowStartTicks = geNow;
                                dmgTallyBh = 0f;
                                dmgTallyEh = 0f;
                                dmgTallyLastDropTicks = 0;
                            }
                        }
                        else if (!sameVeh && autoCollisionLastVehHandle != 0)
                        {
                            // iter-34 BS-1: entered a DIFFERENT vehicle — log the swap
                            // (07-03: both replacement-Tezeract spawns were invisible).
                            driveLogger.Write("[F" + driveLogFrameCount + "] EVENT vehicle-swap:"
                                + " kind=handle oldHandle=" + autoCollisionLastVehHandle
                                + " newHandle=" + logVeh.Handle
                                + " oldBh=" + autoCollisionLastBodyHealth.ToString("F0")
                                + " newBh=" + curBody.ToString("F0")
                                + " model=" + logVeh.DisplayName);
                            grindEpisodeStartTicks = 0;
                        }
                        autoCollisionLastHealth = curH;
                        autoCollisionLastBodyHealth = curBody;
                        autoCollisionLastEngineHealth = curEngine;
                        autoCollisionLastVehHandle = logVeh.Handle;
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        // On foot or aircraft: reset baseline so re-entering a
                        // vehicle doesn't fire a spurious AUTO-COLLISION from
                        // the old health value.
                        autoCollisionLastHealth = -1f;
                        autoCollisionLastBodyHealth = -1f;
                        autoCollisionLastEngineHealth = -1f;
                        autoCollisionLastVehHandle = 0;
                        grindEpisodeStartTicks = 0; // iter-34 BS-2
                    }
                }

                } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("drive assist", ex); }

                // iter-44: intoxicated-driving actuation. MUST run after the block
                // above — SET_CONTROL_VALUE_NEXT_FRAME is last-writer-wins per frame,
                // so running before ApplyCachedSteeringInputs would let drive assist
                // silently overwrite the drunk/blackout inputs.
                try { TickIntoxDriving(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("intox driving", ex); }

                try {
                // ============================================
                // WAYPOINT TRACKING SYSTEM
                // When active, plays directional beeps toward waypoint
                // Interval based on distance (closer = faster beeps)
                // Panned left/right based on direction
                // ============================================
                if (waypointTrackingActive)
                {
                    // Check if waypoint still exists
                    bool waypointExists = Function.Call<bool>(Hash.IS_WAYPOINT_ACTIVE);

                    if (!waypointExists)
                    {
                        waypointTrackingActive = false;
                        Speech.Info("Waypoint cleared");
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        // Get waypoint position using native function
                        int waypointBlipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_FIRST_BLIP_INFO_ID, 8); // 8 = waypoint blip type
                        if (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, waypointBlipHandle))
                        {
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 waypointPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, waypointBlipHandle);
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;

                            // Calculate distance (2D, ignoring height)
                            float dx = waypointPos.X - playerPos.X;
                            float dy = waypointPos.Y - playerPos.Y;
                            float distance = (float)Math.Sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);

                            // Calculate direction to waypoint relative to player heading
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = new GTA.Math.Vector3(forwardVec.Y, -forwardVec.X, 0);
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toWaypoint = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(new GTA.Math.Vector3(dx, dy, 0));

                            float dotForward = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(forwardVec, toWaypoint);
                            float dotRight = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toWaypoint);

                            // Calculate pan (-1 = left, 0 = center, 1 = right)
                            float pan = Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, dotRight));

                            // Calculate beep interval based on distance
                            // Close (< 50m): 200ms, Far (> 500m): 1000ms
                            float distFactor = Math.Min(distance / 500f, 1f);
                            long beepInterval = (long)(2000000 + (distFactor * 8000000)); // 200ms to 1000ms in ticks

                            if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - waypointBeepTicks > beepInterval)
                            {
                                waypointBeepTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                                // Check if waypoint is behind (dotForward < -0.5)
                                bool waypointBehind = (dotForward < -0.5f);

                                // Pitch based on whether we're facing toward or away
                                // Facing toward (dotForward > 0): higher pitch (good)
                                // Facing away (dotForward < 0): lower pitch (turn around)
                                // One octave lower if waypoint is behind
                                float baseFreq = 400 + (dotForward * 200); // 200-600 Hz
                                float freq = waypointBehind ? baseFreq / 2f : baseFreq; // 100-300 Hz if behind

                                // Pan: center for behind, left/right for sides
                                float actualPan = waypointBehind ? 0f : pan;

                                outWaypoint.Stop();
                                waypointBeep.Gain = 0.1;
                                waypointBeep.Frequency = freq;
                                waypointBeep.Type = SignalGeneratorType.Sin; // Smooth tone for waypoint

                                var wpSample = waypointBeep.Take(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(0.1));
                                var wpPanned = new PanningSampleProvider(wpSample) { Pan = actualPan };
                                outWaypoint.Init(wpPanned);
                                outWaypoint.Play();
                            }

                            // Check if arrived (within 10 meters)
                            if (distance < 10f)
                            {
                                waypointTrackingActive = false;
                                Speech.Info("Arrived at waypoint");
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // MISSION BLIP TRACKING SYSTEM
                // Same principle as waypoint but for mission markers
                // ============================================
                if (missionTrackingActive && trackedBlipHandle != -1)
                {
                    // Check if blip still exists
                    if (!Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, trackedBlipHandle))
                    {
                        missionTrackingActive = false;
                        trackedBlipHandle = -1;
                        Speech.Info("Marker cleared");
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, trackedBlipHandle);
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;

                        float dx = blipPos.X - playerPos.X;
                        float dy = blipPos.Y - playerPos.Y;
                        float distance = (float)Math.Sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);

                        // Calculate direction relative to player heading
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = new GTA.Math.Vector3(forwardVec.Y, -forwardVec.X, 0);
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 toBlip = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(new GTA.Math.Vector3(dx, dy, 0));

                        float dotForward = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(forwardVec, toBlip);
                        float dotRight = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toBlip);

                        // Calculate beep interval based on distance
                        float distFactor = Math.Min(distance / 500f, 1f);
                        long beepInterval = (long)(2000000 + (distFactor * 8000000));

                        if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - missionBeepTicks > beepInterval)
                        {
                            missionBeepTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                            bool behind = (dotForward < -0.5f);
                            float pan = behind ? 0f : Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, dotRight));

                            // Use different tone than waypoint (Triangle wave, slightly different pitch)
                            float baseFreq = 350 + (dotForward * 150); // 200-500 Hz
                            float freq = behind ? baseFreq / 2f : baseFreq;

                            outMissionBeep.Stop();
                            missionBeep.Gain = 0.1;
                            missionBeep.Frequency = freq;
                            missionBeep.Type = SignalGeneratorType.Triangle; // Different from waypoint

                            var missionSample = missionBeep.Take(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(0.1));
                            var missionPanned = new PanningSampleProvider(missionSample) { Pan = pan };
                            outMissionBeep.Init(missionPanned);
                            outMissionBeep.Play();
                        }

                        // Check if arrived
                        if (distance < 15f)
                        {
                            missionTrackingActive = false;
                            trackedBlipHandle = -1;
                            Speech.Info("Arrived at marker");
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // TURN-BY-TURN NAVIGATION SYSTEM
                // Announces turns when driving toward waypoint
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("turnByTurnNavigation") == 1 && (waypointTrackingActive || missionTrackingActive) && Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle())
                {
                    Vehicle veh = Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle;
                    if (veh != null && veh.Speed > 2f) // Only when moving
                    {
                        // Check based on vehicle speed (faster = more frequent checks)
                        long turnInterval = (long)(10000000 - Math.Min(veh.Speed / 40f, 1f) * 5000000); // 1000ms to 500ms

                        if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - turnNavTicks > turnInterval)
                        {
                            turnNavTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                            // Get target position (waypoint or mission blip)
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 targetPos = GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero;
                            if (waypointTrackingActive)
                            {
                                int wpHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_FIRST_BLIP_INFO_ID, 8);
                                if (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, wpHandle))
                                    targetPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, wpHandle);
                            }
                            else if (missionTrackingActive && trackedBlipHandle != -1)
                            {
                                targetPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, trackedBlipHandle);
                            }

                            if (targetPos != GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero)
                            {
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = veh.Position;
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = veh.ForwardVector;
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = veh.RightVector;

                                // Calculate direction to target directly
                                // (GPS pathfinding is complex, so we use direct line-of-sight direction)

                                // Calculate direction to target
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 toTarget = targetPos - playerPos;
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 toTargetNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(new GTA.Math.Vector3(toTarget.X, toTarget.Y, 0));

                                float dotForward = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(forwardVec, toTargetNorm);
                                float dotRight = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toTargetNorm);

                                float distance = toTarget.Length();

                                // Calculate time to arrive (rough estimate based on current speed)
                                float speedMps = veh.Speed; // m/s
                                float timeToArrival = speedMps > 0 ? distance / speedMps : float.MaxValue;

                                // Determine turn direction and urgency
                                string turnAnnouncement = "";

                                // If target is significantly to the left or right
                                if (Math.Abs(dotRight) > 0.3f && dotForward < 0.7f)
                                {
                                    // Calculate approximate distance to turn
                                    float turnDistance = distance * Math.Abs(dotForward);

                                    if (dotRight > 0.5f)
                                    {
                                        if (turnDistance < 50f)
                                            turnAnnouncement = "Turn right now";
                                        else if (turnDistance < 100f)
                                            turnAnnouncement = "Turn right in " + ((int)(turnDistance / 10) * 10) + " meters";
                                        else if (turnDistance < 200f)
                                            turnAnnouncement = "Turn right ahead";
                                    }
                                    else if (dotRight < -0.5f)
                                    {
                                        if (turnDistance < 50f)
                                            turnAnnouncement = "Turn left now";
                                        else if (turnDistance < 100f)
                                            turnAnnouncement = "Turn left in " + ((int)(turnDistance / 10) * 10) + " meters";
                                        else if (turnDistance < 200f)
                                            turnAnnouncement = "Turn left ahead";
                                    }
                                    else if (dotRight > 0.3f)
                                    {
                                        if (turnDistance < 100f)
                                            turnAnnouncement = "Bear right";
                                    }
                                    else if (dotRight < -0.3f)
                                    {
                                        if (turnDistance < 100f)
                                            turnAnnouncement = "Bear left";
                                    }
                                }
                                else if (dotForward < -0.3f)
                                {
                                    // Going wrong way
                                    turnAnnouncement = "Turn around";
                                }
                                else if (dotForward > 0.9f && distance < 100f)
                                {
                                    turnAnnouncement = "Continue straight, " + (int)distance + " meters";
                                }

                                // Only announce if different from last announcement
                                if (!string.IsNullOrEmpty(turnAnnouncement) && turnAnnouncement != lastTurnAnnouncement)
                                {
                                    lastTurnAnnouncement = turnAnnouncement;
                                    lastTurnDistance = distance;
                                    Speech.Info(turnAnnouncement);
                                }
                                // Reset if we've moved significantly
                                else if (Math.Abs(distance - lastTurnDistance) > 50f)
                                {
                                    lastTurnAnnouncement = "";
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("navigation cues", ex); }
                try {
                // ============================================
                // ENEMY DETECTION SYSTEM
                // Proactive detection runs in TickProactiveThreatScan() when bodyguard system is active.
                // Fallback: basic detection when bodyguard system is off.
                // Directional beeps are handled below.
                // ============================================

                if (!bodyguardSystemEnabled)
                {
                    // Basic enemy detection when bodyguard system is off
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - enemyCheckTicks > 20000000) // 2 seconds
                    {
                        enemyCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;
                        trackedEnemies.Clear();

                        Ped[] nearbyPeds = World.GetNearbyPeds(Game.Player.Character.Position, 100f);
                        foreach (Ped ped in nearbyPeds)
                        {
                            if (ped == Game.Player.Character || ped.IsDead) continue;
                            if (ped.IsInCombatAgainst(Game.Player.Character))
                                trackedEnemies.Add(ped);
                        }

                        if (trackedEnemies.Count > 0 && trackedEnemies.Count != lastAnnouncedEnemyCount)
                        {
                            Speech.Info(trackedEnemies.Count + " hostile" + (trackedEnemies.Count > 1 ? "s" : "") + " detected");
                        }
                        lastAnnouncedEnemyCount = trackedEnemies.Count;
                    }
                }

                // Play beeps for tracked enemies (every 300ms per closest enemy)
                if (trackedEnemies.Count > 0 && DateTime.Now.Ticks - enemyBeepTicks > 3000000) // 300ms
                {
                    enemyBeepTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                    // Remove dead enemies from tracking
                    trackedEnemies.RemoveAll(p => p == null || p.IsDead || !p.Exists());

                    if (trackedEnemies.Count > 0)
                    {
                        // Find closest enemy
                        Ped closestEnemy = null;
                        float closestDist = float.MaxValue;

                        foreach (Ped enemy in trackedEnemies)
                        {
                            if (enemy == null || !enemy.Exists()) continue;
                            float dist = World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, enemy.Position);
                            if (dist < closestDist)
                            {
                                closestDist = dist;
                                closestEnemy = enemy;
                            }
                        }

                        if (closestEnemy != null)
                        {
                            // Calculate direction
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 enemyPos = closestEnemy.Position;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toEnemy = enemyPos - playerPos;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toEnemyNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(toEnemy);

                            GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = new GTA.Math.Vector3(forwardVec.Y, -forwardVec.X, 0);

                            float dotForward = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(forwardVec, toEnemyNorm);
                            float dotRight = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toEnemyNorm);

                            // Check if enemy is behind (dotForward < -0.5)
                            bool enemyBehind = (dotForward < -0.5f);

                            // Pan: center for behind, left/right for sides
                            float pan = enemyBehind ? 0f : Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, dotRight));

                            // Frequency based on distance (closer = higher pitch = more urgent)
                            // One octave lower for enemies behind (divide by 2)
                            float distFactor = Math.Min(closestDist / 50f, 1f);
                            float baseFreq = 800 - (distFactor * 400); // 400-800 Hz
                            float freq = enemyBehind ? baseFreq / 2f : baseFreq; // 200-400 Hz if behind

                            outEnemy.Stop();
                            enemyBeep.Gain = 0.12;
                            enemyBeep.Frequency = freq;
                            enemyBeep.Type = SignalGeneratorType.SawTooth; // Harsh tone for enemies

                            var enemySample = enemyBeep.Take(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(0.08));
                            var enemyPanned = new PanningSampleProvider(enemySample) { Pan = pan };
                            outEnemy.Init(enemyPanned);
                            outEnemy.Play();
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // PICKUP DETECTION SYSTEM
                // Detects health packs, armor, weapons within 25m
                // Uses pickup.wav with directional panning similar to nav assist
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("pickupDetection") == 1 && pickupSound != null)
                {
                    // Check every 750ms for pickups
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - pickupCheckTicks > 7500000)
                    {
                        pickupCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                        GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 closestPickupPos = GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero;
                        float closestDist = float.MaxValue;
                        string foundPickupType = "";

                        // Common pickup type hashes in GTA V
                        // Health: PICKUP_HEALTH, PICKUP_HEALTH_SNACK, etc.
                        // Armor: PICKUP_ARMOUR_STANDARD, PICKUP_ARMOUR_STANDARD_MP
                        // Weapons: Various PICKUP_WEAPON_* types
                        // Money: PICKUP_MONEY_CASE, PICKUP_MONEY_VARIABLE, etc.
                        uint[] pickupTypes = {
                                0x8F707C18, // PICKUP_HEALTH
								0x483577E8, // PICKUP_HEALTH_SNACK
								0x4BFB42D1, // PICKUP_ARMOUR_STANDARD
								0xCE6B5C74, // PICKUP_MONEY_CASE
								0xCB83E6B1, // PICKUP_MONEY_VARIABLE
								0xE175C698, // PICKUP_MONEY_MED_BAG
								0x1E9A99F8, // PICKUP_MONEY_PAPER_BAG
								0x3F038C30, // PICKUP_MONEY_PURSE
								0xDE78F17E, // PICKUP_MONEY_SECURITY_CASE
								0xBFCBBF17, // PICKUP_WEAPON_PISTOL
								0x1B06D571, // PICKUP_WEAPON_COMBATPISTOL
								0x5EF9FEC4, // PICKUP_WEAPON_SMG
								0xB1415C0E, // PICKUP_WEAPON_MICROSMG
								0x7F7497E5, // PICKUP_WEAPON_ASSAULTRIFLE
								0xF33C83B0, // PICKUP_WEAPON_SHOTGUN
								0x23C1D0A3, // PICKUP_WEAPON_SNIPERRIFLE
								0xC637F23B, // PICKUP_WEAPON_RPG
								0x9C6F0B5C, // PICKUP_WEAPON_GRENADE
								0x2C014CA6, // PICKUP_WEAPON_KNIFE
								0x6C5B941A, // PICKUP_WEAPON_MINIGUN
								0x693583AD, // PICKUP_AMMO_PISTOL
								0x14AAA644, // PICKUP_AMMO_SMG
								0xE4E2B027  // PICKUP_AMMO_RIFLE
							};

                        string[] pickupNames = {
                                "Health", "Health Snack", "Armor",
                                "Money", "Money", "Money Bag", "Money Bag", "Purse", "Security Case",
                                "Pistol", "Combat Pistol", "SMG", "Micro SMG", "Assault Rifle",
                                "Shotgun", "Sniper Rifle", "RPG", "Grenade", "Knife", "Minigun",
                                "Pistol Ammo", "SMG Ammo", "Rifle Ammo"
                            };

                        // Check for each pickup type
                        for (int i = 0; i < pickupTypes.Length; i++)
                        {
                            // Use GET_PICKUP_COORDS to find pickups of this type within range
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 pickupPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_PICKUP_COORDS, (int)pickupTypes[i]);

                            if (pickupPos != GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero)
                            {
                                float dist = World.GetDistance(playerPos, pickupPos);
                                if (dist < 25f && dist < closestDist)
                                {
                                    closestDist = dist;
                                    closestPickupPos = pickupPos;
                                    foundPickupType = pickupNames[i];
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // Also try checking all nearby objects with IS_ANY_PICKUP_OBJECT_NEAR_POINT
                        if (closestPickupPos == GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero)
                        {
                            // Scan nearby props and check if they're pickups
                            Prop[] nearbyProps = World.GetNearbyProps(playerPos, 25f);
                            foreach (Prop prop in nearbyProps)
                            {
                                if (prop == null || !prop.Exists()) continue;

                                // Check if prop model contains pickup-related strings
                                if (hashes.ContainsKey(prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()))
                                {
                                    string modelName = hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].ToLower();
                                    if (modelName.Contains("pickup") || modelName.Contains("health") ||
                                        modelName.Contains("armour") || modelName.Contains("armor") ||
                                        modelName.Contains("money") || modelName.Contains("briefcase"))
                                    {
                                        float dist = World.GetDistance(playerPos, prop.Position);
                                        if (dist < closestDist)
                                        {
                                            closestDist = dist;
                                            closestPickupPos = prop.Position;
                                            foundPickupType = "Item";
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        // If pickup found, play directional sound
                        if (closestPickupPos != GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero)
                        {
                            // Check if it's a new pickup (different position)
                            if (World.GetDistance(closestPickupPos, lastPickupPos) > 2f)
                            {
                                // Announce new pickup
                                Speech.Info(foundPickupType + ", " + (int)closestDist + " meters");
                                lastPickupPos = closestPickupPos;
                                trackedPickupType = foundPickupType;
                                pickupTrackingActive = true;
                            }
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            pickupTrackingActive = false;
                        }
                    }

                    // Play directional beep toward tracked pickup (like nav assist)
                    if (pickupTrackingActive && lastPickupPos != GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero)
                    {
                        // Beep every 400ms
                        if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - pickupBeepTicks > 4000000)
                        {
                            pickupBeepTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                            float dist = World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, lastPickupPos);

                            // Check if still in range
                            if (dist > 25f)
                            {
                                pickupTrackingActive = false;
                                lastPickupPos = GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero;
                            }
                            else if (dist < 2f)
                            {
                                // Arrived at pickup
                                pickupTrackingActive = false;
                                lastPickupPos = GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero;
                                Speech.Info("Pickup nearby");
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                // Calculate pan direction
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 toPickup = lastPickupPos - Game.Player.Character.Position;
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 toPickupNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(toPickup);
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = new GTA.Math.Vector3(forwardVec.Y, -forwardVec.X, 0);

                                float dotForward = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(forwardVec, toPickupNorm);
                                float dotRight = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toPickupNorm);
                                bool behind = (dotForward < -0.5f);
                                float pan = behind ? 0f : Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, dotRight));

                                // Play panned pickup sound
                                outPickup.Stop();
                                pickupSound.Position = 0;
                                var pickupSample = pickupSound.ToSampleProvider();
                                if (pickupSample.WaveFormat.Channels == 1)
                                {
                                    var pickupPanned = new PanningSampleProvider(pickupSample) { Pan = pan };
                                    outPickup.Init(pickupPanned);
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    outPickup.Init(pickupSound);
                                }
                                outPickup.Play();
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // WATER/HAZARD DETECTION SYSTEM
                // Low bass rumble (80-100Hz) for water
                // Smooth descending tone for dropoffs
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("waterHazardDetection") == 1)
                {
                    bool inVeh = Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle();
                    float vehSpeed = inVeh && Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle != null ? Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle.Speed : 0f;

                    // Interval: 1s on foot, 750ms slow, faster as speed increases
                    long waterInterval = 10000000; // 1 second default
                    if (inVeh)
                    {
                        if (vehSpeed < 10f) waterInterval = 7500000; // 750ms slow
                        else waterInterval = (long)(7500000 - Math.Min(vehSpeed / 50f, 1f) * 5000000); // down to 250ms
                    }

                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - waterCheckTicks > waterInterval)
                    {
                        waterCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                        GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = inVeh && Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle != null
                            ? Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle.ForwardVector
                            : Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;

                        // Check ahead for water (10-30m depending on speed)
                        float checkDist = inVeh ? Math.Min(10f + vehSpeed * 0.5f, 30f) : 10f;
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 checkPos = playerPos + (forwardVec * checkDist);

                        // Get ground height at check position
                        float groundZ = World.GetGroundHeight(checkPos);

                        // Check if position is over water
                        bool isWater = (groundZ < 1f && checkPos.Z > groundZ + 5f); // Water if no ground found below

                        if (isWater && !wasNearWater)
                        {
                            // Play low bass rumble
                            outWater.Stop();
                            waterRumble.Frequency = 90; // 80-100 Hz
                            waterRumble.Gain = 0.2;
                            waterRumble.Type = SignalGeneratorType.Sin;
                            var waterSample = waterRumble.Take(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(0.5));
                            outWater.Init(waterSample);
                            outWater.Play();
                            wasNearWater = true;
                        }
                        else if (!isWater)
                        {
                            wasNearWater = false;
                        }

                        // Check for dropoffs (large height difference)
                        float currentGround = World.GetGroundHeight(playerPos);

                        // FIX: Increased threshold to 5m to avoid false positives from road variations
                        // In vehicles at speed, use slightly lower threshold (4m) since we need more warning time
                        float dropThreshold = (inVeh && vehSpeed > 15f) ? 4f : 5f;

                        if (groundZ < currentGround - dropThreshold)
                        {
                            // Corroborate the terrain-mesh reading (GetGroundHeight) with a
                            // downward BSP raycast at the look-ahead point. The mesh can
                            // disagree with the collision the wall-check ray uses and fire
                            // phantom dropoff warnings at cliff/edge seams; require the ray
                            // to also find no ground above the drop threshold.
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 dropDownStart = checkPos + new GTA.Math.Vector3(0, 0, 2f);
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 dropDownEnd = new GTA.Math.Vector3(checkPos.X, checkPos.Y, currentGround - dropThreshold);
                            RaycastResult dropDownCheck = World.Raycast(dropDownStart, dropDownEnd, IntersectFlags.Map, Game.Player.Character);
                            bool rayConfirmsDrop = !dropDownCheck.DidHit;

                            // FIX: Check for wall between player and dropoff using raycast
                            // If there's a wall, the dropoff is behind it and not a real hazard
                            float rayHeight = inVeh ? 0.5f : 1.0f;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 rayStart = playerPos + new GTA.Math.Vector3(0, 0, rayHeight);
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 rayEnd = checkPos + new GTA.Math.Vector3(0, 0, rayHeight);

                            RaycastResult wallCheck = World.Raycast(rayStart, rayEnd, IntersectFlags.Map, Game.Player.Character);

                            // Only warn if NO wall between us and the dropoff
                            // Allow some tolerance - wall must be within 80% of check distance to block warning
                            bool wallBlocking = false;
                            if (wallCheck.DidHit)
                            {
                                float wallDist = World.GetDistance(rayStart, wallCheck.HitPosition);
                                if (wallDist < checkDist * 0.8f)
                                {
                                    wallBlocking = true;
                                }
                            }

                            if (!wallBlocking && rayConfirmsDrop)
                            {
                                // Calculate panning based on direction to drop
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 toCheck = checkPos - playerPos;
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 toCheckNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(new GTA.Math.Vector3(toCheck.X, toCheck.Y, 0));
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = inVeh && Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle != null
                                    ? Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle.RightVector
                                    : new GTA.Math.Vector3(forwardVec.Y, -forwardVec.X, 0);
                                float dropPan = Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toCheckNorm)));

                                // Play panned descending tone
                                outDropoff.Stop();
                                dropoffTone.Frequency = 600;
                                dropoffTone.Gain = 0.12;
                                dropoffTone.Type = SignalGeneratorType.Sin;
                                var dropSample = dropoffTone.Take(TimeSpan.FromSeconds(0.15));
                                var dropPanned = new PanningSampleProvider(dropSample) { Pan = dropPan };
                                outDropoff.Init(dropPanned);
                                outDropoff.Play();

                                // Speak warning for larger drops (increased threshold to 15m for speech)
                                float dropHeight = currentGround - groundZ;
                                if (dropHeight > 15f)
                                {
                                    Speech.Critical("Drop ahead");
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // VEHICLE HEALTH FEEDBACK (Speech)
                // Announces damage at 75%, 50%, 25%, 10%
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("vehicleHealthFeedback") == 1 && Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle())
                {
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - vehicleHealthCheckTicks > 5000000) // 500ms
                    {
                        vehicleHealthCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;
                        Vehicle veh = Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle;

                        if (veh != null)
                        {
                            // Get health values (0-1000 scale typically)
                            float bodyHealth = veh.BodyHealth / 10f; // Convert to percentage
                            float engineHealth = veh.EngineHealth / 10f;
                            float petrolHealth = veh.PetrolTankHealth / 10f;

                            // Reset warnings when entering new vehicle
                            if (veh.BodyHealth > lastVehicleBodyHealth + 100)
                            {
                                for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) { bodyHealthWarnings[i] = false; engineHealthWarnings[i] = false; petrolHealthWarnings[i] = false; }
                            }

                            // Check body health thresholds
                            if (bodyHealth <= 75 && bodyHealth > 50 && !bodyHealthWarnings[0]) { Speech.Ambient("Body 75 percent"); bodyHealthWarnings[0] = true; }
                            else if (bodyHealth <= 50 && bodyHealth > 25 && !bodyHealthWarnings[1]) { Speech.Ambient("Body 50 percent"); bodyHealthWarnings[1] = true; }
                            else if (bodyHealth <= 25 && bodyHealth > 10 && !bodyHealthWarnings[2]) { Speech.Ambient("Body critical, 25 percent"); bodyHealthWarnings[2] = true; }
                            else if (bodyHealth <= 10 && !bodyHealthWarnings[3]) { Speech.Ambient("Body failing, 10 percent!"); bodyHealthWarnings[3] = true; }

                            // Check engine health
                            if (engineHealth <= 75 && engineHealth > 50 && !engineHealthWarnings[0]) { Speech.Ambient("Engine 75 percent"); engineHealthWarnings[0] = true; }
                            else if (engineHealth <= 50 && engineHealth > 25 && !engineHealthWarnings[1]) { Speech.Ambient("Engine 50 percent"); engineHealthWarnings[1] = true; }
                            else if (engineHealth <= 25 && engineHealth > 10 && !engineHealthWarnings[2]) { Speech.Ambient("Engine critical, 25 percent"); engineHealthWarnings[2] = true; }
                            else if (engineHealth <= 10 && !engineHealthWarnings[3]) { Speech.Ambient("Engine failing, 10 percent!"); engineHealthWarnings[3] = true; }

                            // Check petrol tank
                            if (petrolHealth <= 50 && petrolHealth > 25 && !petrolHealthWarnings[1]) { Speech.Ambient("Fuel tank damaged"); petrolHealthWarnings[1] = true; }
                            else if (petrolHealth <= 25 && petrolHealth > 10 && !petrolHealthWarnings[2]) { Speech.Ambient("Fuel tank leaking!"); petrolHealthWarnings[2] = true; }
                            else if (petrolHealth <= 10 && !petrolHealthWarnings[3]) { Speech.Ambient("Fuel tank critical!"); petrolHealthWarnings[3] = true; }

                            lastVehicleBodyHealth = veh.BodyHealth;
                            lastVehicleEngineHealth = veh.EngineHealth;
                            lastVehiclePetrolTankHealth = veh.PetrolTankHealth;
                        }
                    }
                }
                else if (!Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle())
                {
                    // Reset warnings when exiting vehicle
                    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) { bodyHealthWarnings[i] = false; engineHealthWarnings[i] = false; petrolHealthWarnings[i] = false; }
                }

                // ============================================
                // STAMINA/SPRINT FEEDBACK
                // Spoken warning when stamina low
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("staminaFeedback") == 1 && !Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle())
                {
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - staminaCheckTicks > 5000000) // 500ms
                    {
                        staminaCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                        // Get stamina (0-100)
                        float stamina = Function.Call<float>(Hash.GET_PLAYER_SPRINT_STAMINA_REMAINING, Game.Player);

                        if (stamina < 20f && !staminaWarningGiven && Game.Player.Character.IsSprinting)
                        {
                            Speech.Info("Low stamina");
                            staminaWarningGiven = true;
                        }
                        else if (stamina > 50f)
                        {
                            staminaWarningGiven = false;
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // TRAFFIC AWARENESS
                // Spoken warnings for fast-approaching vehicles
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("trafficAwareness") == 1 && Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle())
                {
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - trafficCheckTicks > 5000000) // 500ms
                    {
                        trafficCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                        Vehicle playerVeh = Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle;
                        if (playerVeh != null)
                        {
                            Vehicle[] nearbyVehs = World.GetNearbyVehicles(playerVeh.Position, 50f);

                            foreach (Vehicle veh in nearbyVehs)
                            {
                                if (veh == playerVeh || veh == lastWarnedVehicle) continue;

                                // Check if vehicle is approaching fast
                                float vehSpeed = veh.Speed * 2.236856f; // Convert to MPH
                                if (vehSpeed < 30f) continue; // Only warn for fast vehicles

                                // Check if approaching from sides or behind
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 toVeh = veh.Position - playerVeh.Position;
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 toVehNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(toVeh);
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 vehVelocityNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(veh.Velocity);

                                // Check if vehicle is heading toward us
                                float dotApproach = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(vehVelocityNorm, GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(-toVeh));
                                if (dotApproach < 0.5f) continue; // Not heading toward us

                                // Calculate direction
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = playerVeh.RightVector;
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = playerVeh.ForwardVector;

                                float dotRight = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toVehNorm);
                                float dotForward = GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(forwardVec, toVehNorm);

                                string direction = "";
                                if (dotForward < -0.5f) direction = "behind";
                                else if (dotRight > 0.5f) direction = "right";
                                else if (dotRight < -0.5f) direction = "left";
                                else continue; // In front, less urgent

                                Speech.Info("Vehicle approaching from " + direction);
                                lastWarnedVehicle = veh;
                                break;
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // WANTED LEVEL DETAILS
                // Police positions, helicopter, cop count
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("wantedLevelDetails") == 1 && Game.Player.WantedLevel > 0)
                {
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - wantedDetailsTicks > 50000000) // 5 seconds
                    {
                        wantedDetailsTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                        // Count nearby cops
                        Ped[] nearbyPeds = World.GetNearbyPeds(Game.Player.Character.Position, 100f);
                        int copCount = 0;

                        foreach (Ped ped in nearbyPeds)
                        {
                            if (ped == null || ped.IsDead) continue;
                            if (Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_PED_TYPE, ped) == 6) copCount++;
                        }

                        // Check for police helicopter
                        bool heliPresent = false;
                        Vehicle[] nearbyVehs = World.GetNearbyVehicles(Game.Player.Character.Position, 200f);
                        foreach (Vehicle veh in nearbyVehs)
                        {
                            if (veh != null && (veh.Model.Hash == (int)VehicleHash.Polmav))
                            {
                                heliPresent = true;
                                break;
                            }
                        }

                        string msg = copCount + " cops nearby";
                        if (heliPresent) msg += ", helicopter overhead";
                        Speech.Ambient(msg);
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // SLOPE/TERRAIN FEEDBACK
                // Spoken notification for drastic slope changes
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("slopeTerrainFeedback") == 1 && !Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle())
                {
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - slopeCheckTicks > 10000000) // 1 second
                    {
                        slopeCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                        // Get ground normal to determine slope
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;

                        // Check height difference ahead vs behind
                        float heightAhead = World.GetGroundHeight(playerPos + (forwardVec * 3f));
                        float heightBehind = World.GetGroundHeight(playerPos - (forwardVec * 3f));
                        float currentHeight = World.GetGroundHeight(playerPos);

                        // Calculate slope (height diff over distance)
                        float slope = (heightAhead - currentHeight) / 3f;
                        float slopeAngle = (float)Math.Atan(slope) * 57.2958f; // Convert to degrees

                        // Only announce drastic changes (> 15 degrees difference)
                        if (Math.Abs(slopeAngle - lastGroundSlope) > 15f)
                        {
                            if (slopeAngle > 20f) Speech.Info("Steep uphill");
                            else if (slopeAngle < -20f) Speech.Info("Steep downhill");
                            else if (Math.Abs(slopeAngle) < 5f && Math.Abs(lastGroundSlope) > 15f) Speech.Info("Level ground");
                        }

                        lastGroundSlope = slopeAngle;
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // INTERACTABLE OBJECT DETECTION
                // Spoken alert + directional audio for stores, ATMs, etc.
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("interactableDetection") == 1)
                {
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - interactCheckTicks > 10000000) // 1 second
                    {
                        interactCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                        // Check for nearby interactable blips (stores, missions, etc.)
                        // Blip types: 52 = shop, 207 = barber, 73 = mod shop, etc.
                        int[] interactBlips = { 52, 207, 73, 277, 108, 110, 136, 137, 280 };

                        foreach (int blipType in interactBlips)
                        {
                            int blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_FIRST_BLIP_INFO_ID, blipType);
                            while (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, blipHandle))
                            {
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, blipHandle);
                                float dist = World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, blipPos);

                                if (dist < 20f)
                                {
                                    // Determine type name
                                    string typeName = "Interactable";
                                    if (blipType == 52) typeName = "Shop";
                                    else if (blipType == 207) typeName = "Barber";
                                    else if (blipType == 73) typeName = "Mod Shop";
                                    else if (blipType == 277) typeName = "Clothes Store";
                                    else if (blipType == 108) typeName = "Tattoo Parlor";
                                    else if (blipType == 110) typeName = "Cinema";
                                    else if (blipType == 136 || blipType == 137) typeName = "Mission";

                                    Speech.Info(typeName + ", " + (int)dist + " meters");

                                    // Play directional sound if available
                                    if (interactSound != null)
                                    {
                                        GTA.Math.Vector3 toBlip = blipPos - Game.Player.Character.Position;
                                        GTA.Math.Vector3 toBlipNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(toBlip);
                                        GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;
                                        GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = new GTA.Math.Vector3(forwardVec.Y, -forwardVec.X, 0);
                                        float pan = Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toBlipNorm)));

                                        outInteract.Stop();
                                        interactSound.Position = 0;
                                        outInteract.Init(interactSound);
                                        outInteract.Play();
                                    }
                                    break;
                                }

                                blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_NEXT_BLIP_INFO_ID, blipType);
                            }
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // COVER DETECTION (Combat)
                // Uses cover.wav with directional panning
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("coverDetection") == 1 && coverSound != null && trackedEnemies.Count > 0)
                {
                    if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - coverCheckTicks > 20000000) // 2 seconds
                    {
                        coverCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                        // Find nearby cover points using raycasts
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = new GTA.Math.Vector3(forwardVec.Y, -forwardVec.X, 0);

                        // Check 8 directions for cover
                        GTA.Math.Vector3[] directions = {
                                forwardVec, -forwardVec, rightVec, -rightVec,
                                GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(forwardVec + rightVec),
                                GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(forwardVec - rightVec),
                                GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(-forwardVec + rightVec),
                                GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(-forwardVec - rightVec)
                            };

                        GTA.Math.Vector3 bestCover = GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero;
                        float bestCoverDist = float.MaxValue;

                        foreach (GTA.Math.Vector3 dir in directions)
                        {
                            RaycastResult ray = World.Raycast(playerPos + new GTA.Math.Vector3(0, 0, 0.5f),
                                playerPos + new GTA.Math.Vector3(0, 0, 0.5f) + (dir * 10f),
                                IntersectFlags.Map, Game.Player.Character);

                            if (ray.DidHit)
                            {
                                float dist = World.GetDistance(playerPos, ray.HitPosition);
                                if (dist > 2f && dist < bestCoverDist)
                                {
                                    bestCoverDist = dist;
                                    bestCover = ray.HitPosition;
                                }
                            }
                        }

                        if (bestCover != GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero && bestCoverDist < 8f)
                        {
                            // Calculate pan direction
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toCover = bestCover - playerPos;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toCoverNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(toCover);
                            float pan = Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toCoverNorm)));

                            outCover.Stop();
                            coverSound.Position = 0;
                            outCover.Init(coverSound);
                            outCover.Play();
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // BATCH 2 FEATURES - Combat Feedback
                // ============================================

                // Combat Hit/Headshot/Kill Detection (50ms interval)
                if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - combatCheckTicks > 500000) // 50ms
                {
                    combatCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                    // Get all nearby peds
                    Ped[] nearbyPeds = World.GetNearbyPeds(Game.Player.Character.Position, 50f);
                    List<int> currentPedHandles = new List<int>();

                    foreach (Ped ped in nearbyPeds)
                    {
                        if (ped == null || ped == Game.Player.Character) continue;

                        int handle = ped.Handle;
                        currentPedHandles.Add(handle);
                        int currentHealth = ped.Health;

                        // Check if we're tracking this ped
                        if (pedHealthTracker.ContainsKey(handle))
                        {
                            int previousHealth = pedHealthTracker[handle];

                            // Check if health decreased (we hit them)
                            if (currentHealth < previousHealth)
                            {
                                // Verify we damaged them
                                if (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.HAS_ENTITY_BEEN_DAMAGED_BY_ENTITY, ped, Game.Player.Character, true))
                                {
                                    if (currentHealth <= 0)
                                    {
                                        // Kill!
                                        if (killSound != null && outKill != null)
                                        {
                                            outKill.Stop();
                                            killSound.Position = 0;
                                            outKill.Init(killSound);
                                            outKill.Play();
                                        }
                                    }
                                    else
                                    {
                                        // Check for headshot using native function to get last damaged bone
                                        OutputArgument boneArg = new OutputArgument();
                                        Function.Call(Hash.GET_PED_LAST_DAMAGE_BONE, ped, boneArg);
                                        int lastBone = boneArg.GetResult<int>();
                                        // Head bone IDs: 31086 (SKEL_Head), 12844 (IK_Head)
                                        bool isHeadshot = (lastBone == 31086 || lastBone == 12844);

                                        if (isHeadshot && headshotSound != null && outHeadshot != null)
                                        {
                                            outHeadshot.Stop();
                                            headshotSound.Position = 0;
                                            outHeadshot.Init(headshotSound);
                                            outHeadshot.Play();
                                        }
                                        else if (hitSound != null && outHit != null)
                                        {
                                            outHit.Stop();
                                            hitSound.Position = 0;
                                            outHit.Init(hitSound);
                                            outHit.Play();
                                        }
                                    }
                                }
                            }

                            // Update health
                            pedHealthTracker[handle] = currentHealth;
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            // Start tracking this ped
                            pedHealthTracker[handle] = currentHealth;
                        }
                    }

                    // Clean up dead/distant peds from tracker
                    List<int> toRemove = new List<int>();
                    foreach (int handle in pedHealthTracker.Keys)
                    {
                        if (!currentPedHandles.Contains(handle))
                            toRemove.Add(handle);
                    }
                    foreach (int handle in toRemove)
                    {
                        pedHealthTracker.Remove(handle);
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // BATCH 2 FEATURES - Vehicle Entry Detection
                // ============================================
                bool currentlyInVehicle = Game.Player.Character.IsInVehicle();
                if (currentlyInVehicle && !wasInVehicle)
                {
                    // Just entered a vehicle
                    Vehicle veh = Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle;
                    if (veh != null && veh != lastEnteredVehicle)
                    {
                        string vehName = veh.LocalizedName;
                        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(vehName) || vehName == "NULL")
                            vehName = veh.DisplayName;
                        Speech.Info("Entering " + vehName);
                        lastEnteredVehicle = veh;
                    }
                }
                wasInVehicle = currentlyInVehicle;

                // Passenger Count Detection (2s interval, on foot only)
                if (!currentlyInVehicle && DateTime.Now.Ticks - passengerCheckTicks > 20000000) // 2 seconds
                {
                    passengerCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                    Vehicle[] nearbyVehs = World.GetNearbyVehicles(Game.Player.Character.Position, 5f);
                    Vehicle closestOccupied = null;
                    float closestDist = float.MaxValue;
                    int occupantCount = 0;

                    foreach (Vehicle veh in nearbyVehs)
                    {
                        if (veh == null) continue;

                        // Count occupants
                        int count = 0;
                        // Check driver seat (-1) and passenger seats (0 to PassengerCapacity-1)
                        if (veh.Driver != null && veh.Driver.IsAlive) count++;
                        for (int seat = 0; seat < veh.PassengerCapacity; seat++)
                        {
                            Ped passenger = veh.GetPedOnSeat((VehicleSeat)seat);
                            if (passenger != null && passenger.IsAlive) count++;
                        }

                        if (count > 0)
                        {
                            float dist = World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, veh.Position);
                            if (dist < closestDist)
                            {
                                closestDist = dist;
                                closestOccupied = veh;
                                occupantCount = count;
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    if (closestOccupied != null && occupantCount > 0)
                    {
                        string vehName = closestOccupied.LocalizedName;
                        if (string.IsNullOrEmpty(vehName) || vehName == "NULL")
                            vehName = closestOccupied.DisplayName;
                        Speech.Info(vehName + " with " + occupantCount + " occupant" + (occupantCount > 1 ? "s" : ""));
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // BATCH 2 FEATURES - Indoor/Outdoor Detection
                // ============================================
                if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - indoorCheckTicks > 10000000) // 1 second
                {
                    indoorCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                    int interior = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_INTERIOR_FROM_ENTITY, Game.Player.Character);
                    bool isIndoors = (interior != 0);

                    if (isIndoors && !wasIndoors)
                    {
                        Speech.Info("Indoors");
                    }
                    else if (!isIndoors && wasIndoors)
                    {
                        Speech.Info("Outdoors");
                    }
                    wasIndoors = isIndoors;
                }

                // ============================================
                // BATCH 2 FEATURES - Swimming Depth Detection
                // ============================================
                if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - swimCheckTicks > 20000000) // 2 seconds
                {
                    swimCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                    bool isSwimming = Game.Player.Character.IsSwimming || Game.Player.Character.IsSwimmingUnderWater;

                    if (isSwimming && Game.Player.Character.IsSwimmingUnderWater)
                    {
                        // Calculate depth
                        GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                        float waterSurfaceZ = 0f;
                        bool gotWaterHeight = Function.Call<bool>(Hash.GET_WATER_HEIGHT, playerPos.X, playerPos.Y, playerPos.Z + 50f, (OutputArgument)(new OutputArgument()));

                        // Use output argument to get water height
                        OutputArgument waterHeightArg = new OutputArgument();
                        if (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.GET_WATER_HEIGHT, playerPos.X, playerPos.Y, playerPos.Z + 50f, waterHeightArg))
                        {
                            waterSurfaceZ = waterHeightArg.GetResult<float>();
                            float depth = waterSurfaceZ - playerPos.Z;
                            if (depth > 0)
                            {
                                int depthMeters = (int)Math.Round(depth);
                                if (!wasSwimming || depthMeters > 1)
                                {
                                    Speech.Info(depthMeters + " meters deep");
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    wasSwimming = isSwimming;
                }

                // ============================================
                // BATCH 2 FEATURES - Door/Ladder Audio Detection
                // ============================================
                if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - doorLadderCheckTicks > 7500000) // 750ms
                {
                    doorLadderCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;
                    float scanRadius = Math.Min(GetDetectionRadius(), 15f);

                    Prop[] props = World.GetNearbyProps(Game.Player.Character.Position, scanRadius);
                    GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                    GTA.Math.Vector3 forwardVec = Game.Player.Character.ForwardVector;
                    GTA.Math.Vector3 rightVec = new GTA.Math.Vector3(forwardVec.Y, -forwardVec.X, 0);

                    foreach (Prop prop in props)
                    {
                        if (prop == null || !prop.IsVisible) continue;

                        float dist = World.GetDistance(playerPos, prop.Position);
                        if (dist > 5f) continue; // Only within 5m for audio

                        // Check if it's a door or ladder
                        string modelName = "";
                        if (hashes.ContainsKey(prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()))
                            modelName = hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].ToLower();

                        bool isDoor = modelName.Contains("door") || modelName.Contains("gate");
                        bool isLadder = modelName.Contains("ladder");

                        if (isDoor && prop != lastAnnouncedDoor && doorSound != null && outDoor != null)
                        {
                            // Calculate pan
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toObj = prop.Position - playerPos;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toObjNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(toObj);
                            float pan = Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toObjNorm)));

                            outDoor.Stop();
                            doorSound.Position = 0;
                            // Apply panning if mono
                            if (doorSound.WaveFormat.Channels == 1)
                            {
                                var panned = new PanningSampleProvider(doorSound.ToSampleProvider()) { Pan = pan };
                                outDoor.Init(panned);
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                outDoor.Init(doorSound);
                            }
                            outDoor.Play();
                            lastAnnouncedDoor = prop;
                        }
                        else if (isLadder && prop != lastAnnouncedLadder && ladderSound != null && outLadder != null)
                        {
                            // Calculate pan
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toObj = prop.Position - playerPos;
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 toObjNorm = GTA.Math.Vector3.Normalize(toObj);
                            float pan = Math.Max(-1f, Math.Min(1f, GTA.Math.Vector3.Dot(rightVec, toObjNorm)));

                            outLadder.Stop();
                            ladderSound.Position = 0;
                            if (ladderSound.WaveFormat.Channels == 1)
                            {
                                var panned = new PanningSampleProvider(ladderSound.ToSampleProvider()) { Pan = pan };
                                outLadder.Init(panned);
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                outLadder.Init(ladderSound);
                            }
                            outLadder.Play();
                            lastAnnouncedLadder = prop;
                        }
                    }

                    // Reset announcements if we've moved away
                    if (lastAnnouncedDoor != null && World.GetDistance(playerPos, lastAnnouncedDoor.Position) > 8f)
                        lastAnnouncedDoor = null;
                    if (lastAnnouncedLadder != null && World.GetDistance(playerPos, lastAnnouncedLadder.Position) > 8f)
                        lastAnnouncedLadder = null;
                }

                // ============================================
                // BATCH 2 FEATURES - Safe House Proximity
                // ============================================
                if (DateTime.Now.Ticks - safeHouseCheckTicks > 50000000) // 5 seconds
                {
                    safeHouseCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                    // Determine current character
                    PedHash playerHash = (PedHash)Game.Player.Character.Model.Hash;
                    GTA.Math.Vector3 safeHousePos = GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero;
                    string safeHouseName = "";

                    if (playerHash == PedHash.Michael)
                    {
                        safeHousePos = new GTA.Math.Vector3(-852.4f, 160.0f, 65.6f);
                        safeHouseName = "Michael's safe house";
                    }
                    else if (playerHash == PedHash.Franklin)
                    {
                        safeHousePos = new GTA.Math.Vector3(7.9f, 548.1f, 175.5f);
                        safeHouseName = "Franklin's safe house";
                    }
                    else if (playerHash == PedHash.Trevor)
                    {
                        safeHousePos = new GTA.Math.Vector3(1985.7f, 3812.2f, 32.2f);
                        safeHouseName = "Trevor's safe house";
                    }

                    if (safeHousePos != GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero)
                    {
                        float dist = World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, safeHousePos);

                        if (dist < 50f && !nearSafeHouseAnnounced)
                        {
                            Speech.Info(safeHouseName + " nearby");
                            nearSafeHouseAnnounced = true;
                        }
                        else if (dist > 100f)
                        {
                            nearSafeHouseAnnounced = false;
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // BATCH 2 FEATURES - Service Proximity
                // ============================================
                if (getSetting("serviceProximity") == 1 && DateTime.Now.Ticks - serviceCheckTicks > 30000000) // 3 seconds
                {
                    serviceCheckTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;

                    // Service blip types: 110=Ammu-Nation, 61=Hospital, 408=Clothing, 73=Mod Shop, 207=Barber, 362=Tattoo, 89=ATM
                    int[] serviceTypes = { 110, 61, 408, 73, 207, 362, 89 };
                    string[] serviceNames = { "Ammu-Nation", "Hospital", "Clothing Store", "Mod Shop", "Barber", "Tattoo Parlor", "ATM" };

                    float userRadius = GetDetectionRadius();
                    GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;

                    // Reset announcement if player moved far from last announced service
                    if (lastAnnouncedServiceBlip != -1 && lastAnnouncedServicePos != GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero)
                    {
                        float distToLast = World.GetDistance(playerPos, lastAnnouncedServicePos);
                        if (distToLast > userRadius * 1.5f)
                        {
                            lastAnnouncedServiceBlip = -1;
                            lastAnnouncedServicePos = GTA.Math.Vector3.Zero;
                        }
                    }

                    for (int i = 0; i < serviceTypes.Length; i++)
                    {
                        int blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_FIRST_BLIP_INFO_ID, serviceTypes[i]);
                        while (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, blipHandle))
                        {
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, blipHandle);
                            float dist = World.GetDistance(playerPos, blipPos);

                            if (dist < userRadius && blipHandle != lastAnnouncedServiceBlip)
                            {
                                // Calculate direction
                                float dx = blipPos.X - playerPos.X;
                                float dy = blipPos.Y - playerPos.Y;
                                // iter-37 N12: -dx converts the clockwise atan2 bearing to the
                            // counterclockwise (GTA-heading) convention getDir expects —
                            // east/west were mirrored in every spoken blip direction.
                            double angle = Math.Atan2(-dx, dy) * (180.0 / Math.PI);
                                if (angle < 0) angle += 360;

                                string direction = getDir((float)angle);
                                Speech.Info(serviceNames[i] + ", " + (int)dist + " meters " + direction);
                                lastAnnouncedServiceBlip = blipHandle;
                                lastAnnouncedServicePos = blipPos;
                                break;
                            }

                            blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_NEXT_BLIP_INFO_ID, serviceTypes[i]);
                        }
                    }
                }
                } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("world feedback", ex); }

            }

            // Arbitrate and emit any priority-queued speech requested this tick.
            // iter-37: nav output layer per-tick pass — pulse emitter, deferred
            // BEHIND double-ticks, query-key state machine. Runs before the
            // speech drain so query snapshots requested this tick are voiced
            // this tick.
            try { NavAssistAudioTick(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("nav audio", ex); }
            try { DrainNavBeepQueue(); } catch { }
            try { NavQueryTick(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("nav query", ex); }
            try { NavGuidanceTick(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("nav guidance", ex); }
            // Menu Reader + menulog probe. Deliberately NOT gated on
            // Game.IsPaused — they only work because onTick keeps firing while
            // the (unpaused) pause menu is up. Shared state is captured once
            // (one-frame natives are consume-on-read), then the probe logs and
            // the reader speaks. All before Speech.Drain so announcements are
            // voiced this tick.
            try { TickFrontendShared(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("frontend state", ex); }
            try { TickMenuProbe(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("menu probe", ex); }
            try { TickMenuReader(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("menu reader", ex); }
            // iter-52. The packed-stat sweep only runs while collectible navigation is
            // on, and stops for good once it has swept its window — it is calibration,
            // not a per-frame cost.
            if (getSetting("collectibleNav") == 1)
                try { TickPackedStatScan(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("collectible stats", ex); }
            try { TickTargetHoming(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("target homing", ex); }
            try { TickRestrictedAreas(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("restricted areas", ex); }
            try { TickEventsAndServices(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("events and services", ex); }
            try { TickSnapshotPreroll(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("snapshot preroll", ex); }
            try { TickInteractionCatalogue(); } catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("interaction catalogue", ex); }
            try { Speech.Drain(); } catch { }
        }

        // Exception shield: onKeyDown/onKeyUp had no protection, so a single
        // throw inside any menu/scan handler propagated out and SHVDN aborted
        // the whole script — a blind player instantly loses ALL audio guidance.
        // Same pattern as the per-subsystem try/catch in onTick. keyState[]
        // flags left set by a mid-handler throw self-heal via onKeyUp.
        private void onKeyDown(object sender, KeyEventArgs e)
        {
            try { onKeyDownCore(sender, e); }
            catch (Exception ex) { ReportSubsystemError("keydown", ex); }
        }

        private void onKeyDownCore(object sender, KeyEventArgs e)
        {

            if (e.Control)
            {
                shifting = true;
            }

            /*
			if (e.KeyCode == Keys.NumPad7 && !shifting && !keyState[7])
			{
				keyState[7] = true;
				Vehicle[] vehicles = World.GetNearbyVehicles(Game.Player.Character.Position, 500);
				foreach (Vehicle vehicle in vehicles)
				{
					if (vehicle.IsDead == false)
					{
						vehicle.Explode();

					}
				}


			}
			*/

            if (e.KeyCode == Keys.NumPad2 && shifting && !keyState[2])
            {
                keyState[2] = true;

                if (!keys_disabled)
                {
                    keys_disabled = true;
                    Speech.Ambient("Accessibility keys deactivated.");
                }
                else if (keys_disabled)
                {
                    keys_disabled = false;
                    Speech.Ambient("Accessibility keys activated.");
                }
            }

            if (!keys_disabled)
            {
                // F1 — player-indicated failure marker for drive-assist debugging.
                // A play-tester presses this to stamp the current failure moment
                // into the drive-assist debug log.
                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.F1 && !keyState[18])
                {
                    keyState[18] = true;
                    LogPlayerIndicatedFailure();
                }

                // Menulog spike2: Esc opens the REAL pause menu WITHOUT pausing,
                // so scripts keep ticking and the pause probe can run against it
                // (the SP pause menu suspends all SHV scripts — spike1 log proved
                // it: a 52 s tick hole while paused). Only active while
                // menuDebugLog is on. P still opens the normal paused menu —
                // TickPauseProbe disables only control 200 (Esc), not 199 (P).
                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.Escape && (menuLogWasEnabled || mrReaderEnabled) && !keyState[21])
                {
                    keyState[21] = true;
                    // 500 ms cooldown: SHVDN can deliver several queued KeyDowns
                    // in one frame BEFORE the menu reports active (spike3 log:
                    // 4 duplicate frontend-open calls in a single frame).
                    if (!Function.Call<bool>(Hash.IS_PAUSE_MENU_ACTIVE)
                        && (DateTime.Now - mrLastFrontendOpenAt).TotalMilliseconds >= 500)
                    {
                        mrLastFrontendOpenAt = DateTime.Now;
                        // v1.2: the OPENING Esc press must not reach the
                        // frontend as CANCEL (held key = instant self-close in
                        // every v1.1 open of one session). Hold-off runs until
                        // this press's KeyUp + 150 ms grace.
                        mrEscHoldoff = true;
                        mrEscHoldoffEnd = DateTime.MaxValue;
                        mrCtrlHeld[5] = true; // pre-seed cancel held-state: no spurious edge event
                        Function.Call(Hash.ACTIVATE_FRONTEND_MENU,
                            Game.GenerateHash("FE_MENU_VERSION_SP_PAUSE"), false, -1);
                        MLog("EVENT frontend-open: version=FE_MENU_VERSION_SP_PAUSE pause=0");
                    }
                }

                // v1.2 Menu Reader input capture — OS key events are the
                // primary nav-input source in the hijacked frontend (control
                // natives report false for nav controls there). Deliberately
                // NOT keyState-debounced: OS auto-repeat must pass through.
                if (menuLogWasEnabled || mrReaderEnabled)
                {
                    switch (e.KeyCode)
                    {
                        case Keys.Up: case Keys.W: mrKeyInputBits |= MR_IN_UP; break;
                        case Keys.Down: case Keys.S: mrKeyInputBits |= MR_IN_DOWN; break;
                        case Keys.Left: case Keys.A: mrKeyInputBits |= MR_IN_LEFT; break;
                        case Keys.Right: case Keys.D: mrKeyInputBits |= MR_IN_RIGHT; break;
                        case Keys.Enter: mrKeyInputBits |= MR_IN_ACCEPT; break;
                        case Keys.Back: mrKeyInputBits |= MR_IN_CANCEL; break;
                        case Keys.Escape:
                            if (!mrEscHoldoff) mrKeyInputBits |= MR_IN_CANCEL;
                            break;
                    }
                }

                // iter-37: NumPad Divide — nav-assist query key. Tap = Around Me,
                // double-tap = What's Ahead, hold = Where Am I. The tap/double/
                // hold discrimination lives in NavQueryTick + onKeyUp; here we
                // only stamp the press.
                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.Divide && !keyState[20])
                {
                    keyState[20] = true;
                    navQueryKeyIsDown = true;
                    navQueryHoldFired = false;
                    navQueryKeyDownTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;
                }

                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.NumPad4 && !keyState[4])
                {
                    keyState[4] = true;
                    float detectRadius = GetDetectionRadius();
                    Vehicle[] vehicles = World.GetNearbyVehicles(Game.Player.Character.Position, detectRadius);
                    string status;
                    List<Result> results = new List<Result>();
                    bool valid = false;
                    foreach (Vehicle vehicle in vehicles)
                    {
                        valid = false;

                        if (getSetting("onscreen") == 0 && vehicle.IsVisible && !vehicle.IsDead)
                            valid = true;

                        if (getSetting("onscreen") == 1 && vehicle.IsVisible && !vehicle.IsDead && vehicle.IsOnScreen)
                            valid = true;

                        if (valid)
                        {
                            if (vehicle.IsStopped)
                            {
                                status = "a stationary";
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                status = "a moving";
                            }
                            if (Game.Player.Character.CurrentVehicle != vehicle)
                            {
                                string name = (status + " " + vehicle.LocalizedName);
                                double xyDistance = Math.Round(World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, vehicle.Position) - Math.Abs(Game.Player.Character.Position.Z - vehicle.Position.Z), 1);
                                double zDistance = Math.Round(vehicle.Position.Z - Game.Player.Character.Position.Z, 1);
                                string direction = getDir(calculate_x_y_angle(Game.Player.Character.Position.X, Game.Player.Character.Position.Y, vehicle.Position.X, vehicle.Position.Y, 0));
                                Result result = new Result(name, xyDistance, zDistance, direction);
                                results.Add(result);
                            }

                        }
                    }

                    Speech.Ambient(listToString(results, "Nearest Vehicles: "));

                }


                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.Decimal && !keyState[10])
                {
                    keyState[10] = true;

                    // Double-tap detection: 250ms window
                    long currentTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;
                    bool isDoubleTap = (currentTicks - lastDecimalPressTicks) < 2500000; // 250ms in ticks
                    lastDecimalPressTicks = currentTicks;

                    if (isDoubleTap)
                    {
                        // DOUBLE TAP: Toggle waypoint/mission tracking
                        // Check if waypoint exists
                        bool waypointExists = Function.Call<bool>(Hash.IS_WAYPOINT_ACTIVE);

                        if (waypointExists)
                        {
                            // Toggle waypoint tracking
                            if (waypointTrackingActive)
                            {
                                waypointTrackingActive = false;
                                Speech.Info("Waypoint tracking stopped");
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                // Start tracking and announce distance/direction
                                int waypointBlipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_FIRST_BLIP_INFO_ID, 8); // 8 = waypoint blip type
                                if (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, waypointBlipHandle))
                                {
                                    GTA.Math.Vector3 waypointPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, waypointBlipHandle);
                                    GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;

                                    // Calculate distance
                                    float dx = waypointPos.X - playerPos.X;
                                    float dy = waypointPos.Y - playerPos.Y;
                                    float distance = (float)Math.Sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);

                                    // Calculate direction to waypoint
                                    // iter-37 N12: -dx — see the compass-convention note at getDir.
                                    double angleToWaypoint = Math.Atan2(-dx, dy) * (180.0 / Math.PI);
                                    if (angleToWaypoint < 0) angleToWaypoint += 360;

                                    string direction = getDir((float)angleToWaypoint);
                                    int distMeters = (int)Math.Round(distance);

                                    waypointTrackingActive = true;
                                    missionTrackingActive = false; // Disable mission tracking
                                    waypointBeepTicks = 0; // Reset to play beep immediately
                                    Speech.Info("Waypoint tracking. " + distMeters + " meters " + direction);
                                }
                            }
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            // No waypoint - scan for mission/objective blips
                            // If already tracking, toggle off
                            if (missionTrackingActive)
                            {
                                missionTrackingActive = false;
                                trackedBlipHandle = -1;
                                Speech.Info("Mission tracking stopped");
                            }
                            else
                            {
                                // Scan for available blips
                                int[] missionBlipTypes = { 1, 2, 66, 143, 225, 304, 305, 407, 417, 478 };
                                string[] blipTypeNames = { "Destination", "Vehicle", "Mission", "Gang Attack",
                                    "Stranger", "Objective", "Crew", "Boss", "Crew Member", "Activity" };

                                GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                                float closestDist = float.MaxValue;
                                int closestBlipHandle = -1;
                                string closestBlipName = "";
                                int foundCount = 0;
                                List<string> foundBlips = new List<string>();

                                for (int i = 0; i < missionBlipTypes.Length; i++)
                                {
                                    int blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_FIRST_BLIP_INFO_ID, missionBlipTypes[i]);
                                    while (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, blipHandle))
                                    {
                                        GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, blipHandle);
                                        float dist = World.GetDistance(playerPos, blipPos);

                                        foundCount++;
                                        if (!foundBlips.Contains(blipTypeNames[i]))
                                            foundBlips.Add(blipTypeNames[i]);

                                        if (dist < closestDist)
                                        {
                                            closestDist = dist;
                                            closestBlipHandle = blipHandle;
                                            closestBlipName = blipTypeNames[i];
                                            trackedBlipType = missionBlipTypes[i];
                                        }

                                        blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_NEXT_BLIP_INFO_ID, missionBlipTypes[i]);
                                    }
                                }

                                if (closestBlipHandle != -1)
                                {
                                    // Start tracking nearest blip
                                    trackedBlipHandle = closestBlipHandle;
                                    missionTrackingActive = true;
                                    missionBeepTicks = 0;

                                    // Calculate direction
                                    GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, closestBlipHandle);
                                    float dx = blipPos.X - playerPos.X;
                                    float dy = blipPos.Y - playerPos.Y;
                                    // iter-37 N12: -dx converts the clockwise atan2 bearing to the
                            // counterclockwise (GTA-heading) convention getDir expects —
                            // east/west were mirrored in every spoken blip direction.
                            double angle = Math.Atan2(-dx, dy) * (180.0 / Math.PI);
                                    if (angle < 0) angle += 360;

                                    string foundList = foundBlips.Count > 1 ? String.Join(", ", foundBlips.Take(3)) : closestBlipName;
                                    Speech.Info("Tracking " + closestBlipName + ". " + (int)closestDist + " meters " + getDir((float)angle) +
                                        (foundCount > 1 ? ". " + foundCount + " markers found: " + foundList : ""));
                                }
                                else
                                {
                                    // No markers found
                                    Speech.Info("No markers found");
                                }
                            }
                        }
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        // SINGLE TAP: Just announce current heading
                        Speech.Info("Facing " + getDir(Game.Player.Character.Heading));
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // BLIP CYCLING (NumPad Plus)
                // Cycles through ALL mission markers on map
                // Auto-places waypoint on selected marker
                // ============================================
                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.Add && !keyState[11])
                {
                    keyState[11] = true;

                    // Blip types to scan: mission markers, objectives, destinations, etc.
                    int[] missionBlipTypes = { 1, 2, 66, 143, 225, 304, 305, 407, 417, 478 };
                    string[] blipTypeNames = { "Destination", "Vehicle", "Mission", "Gang Attack",
                        "Stranger", "Objective", "Crew", "Boss", "Crew Member", "Activity" };

                    // Refresh blip list every 2 seconds to catch new markers
                    long currentTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;
                    if (currentTicks - lastBlipScanTicks > 20000000) // 2 seconds
                    {
                        lastBlipScanTicks = currentTicks;
                        availableBlipHandles.Clear();
                        availableBlipNames.Clear();
                        availableBlipTypes.Clear();
                        blipCycleIndex = -1; // Reset index when rescanning

                        GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;

                        // Build sorted list of all available blips
                        List<Tuple<int, string, int, float>> allBlips = new List<Tuple<int, string, int, float>>();

                        for (int i = 0; i < missionBlipTypes.Length; i++)
                        {
                            int blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_FIRST_BLIP_INFO_ID, missionBlipTypes[i]);
                            while (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, blipHandle))
                            {
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, blipHandle);
                                float dist = World.GetDistance(playerPos, blipPos);
                                allBlips.Add(new Tuple<int, string, int, float>(blipHandle, blipTypeNames[i], missionBlipTypes[i], dist));

                                blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_NEXT_BLIP_INFO_ID, missionBlipTypes[i]);
                            }
                        }

                        // Sort by distance (closest first)
                        allBlips.Sort((a, b) => a.Item4.CompareTo(b.Item4));

                        // Store in parallel lists
                        foreach (var blip in allBlips)
                        {
                            availableBlipHandles.Add(blip.Item1);
                            availableBlipNames.Add(blip.Item2);
                            availableBlipTypes.Add(blip.Item3);
                        }
                    }

                    if (availableBlipHandles.Count == 0)
                    {
                        Speech.Info("No markers found");
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        // Cycle to next marker
                        blipCycleIndex++;
                        if (blipCycleIndex >= availableBlipHandles.Count)
                            blipCycleIndex = 0; // Wrap around

                        int selectedHandle = availableBlipHandles[blipCycleIndex];
                        string selectedName = availableBlipNames[blipCycleIndex];
                        int selectedType = availableBlipTypes[blipCycleIndex];

                        // Verify blip still exists
                        if (!Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, selectedHandle))
                        {
                            // Force rescan on next press
                            lastBlipScanTicks = 0;
                            Speech.Info("Marker no longer available, rescanning");
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, selectedHandle);
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;

                            // Calculate distance and direction
                            float dx = blipPos.X - playerPos.X;
                            float dy = blipPos.Y - playerPos.Y;
                            float distance = (float)Math.Sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);
                            // iter-37 N12: -dx converts the clockwise atan2 bearing to the
                            // counterclockwise (GTA-heading) convention getDir expects —
                            // east/west were mirrored in every spoken blip direction.
                            double angle = Math.Atan2(-dx, dy) * (180.0 / Math.PI);
                            if (angle < 0) angle += 360;

                            string direction = getDir((float)angle);

                            // Place waypoint at blip location
                            Function.Call(Hash.SET_NEW_WAYPOINT, blipPos.X, blipPos.Y);

                            // Start tracking this marker
                            trackedBlipHandle = selectedHandle;
                            trackedBlipType = selectedType;
                            missionTrackingActive = true;
                            waypointTrackingActive = true; // Also enable waypoint tracking since we set a waypoint
                            missionBeepTicks = 0;
                            waypointBeepTicks = 0;

                            // Announce: marker X of Y, type, distance, direction
                            string announcement = "Marker " + (blipCycleIndex + 1) + " of " + availableBlipHandles.Count +
                                ". " + selectedName + ", " + (int)distance + " meters " + direction + ". Waypoint set.";
                            Speech.Info(announcement);
                        }
                    }
                }

                // ============================================
                // BLIP CYCLING REVERSE (NumPad Minus)
                // Cycles backwards through mission markers
                // ============================================
                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.Subtract && !keyState[12])
                {
                    keyState[12] = true;

                    // Same blip scanning logic as NumPad Plus
                    int[] missionBlipTypes = { 1, 2, 66, 143, 225, 304, 305, 407, 417, 478 };
                    string[] blipTypeNames = { "Destination", "Vehicle", "Mission", "Gang Attack",
                        "Stranger", "Objective", "Crew", "Boss", "Crew Member", "Activity" };

                    // Refresh blip list every 2 seconds
                    long currentTicks = DateTime.Now.Ticks;
                    if (currentTicks - lastBlipScanTicks > 20000000)
                    {
                        lastBlipScanTicks = currentTicks;
                        availableBlipHandles.Clear();
                        availableBlipNames.Clear();
                        availableBlipTypes.Clear();
                        blipCycleIndex = -1;

                        GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;
                        List<Tuple<int, string, int, float>> allBlips = new List<Tuple<int, string, int, float>>();

                        for (int i = 0; i < missionBlipTypes.Length; i++)
                        {
                            int blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_FIRST_BLIP_INFO_ID, missionBlipTypes[i]);
                            while (Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, blipHandle))
                            {
                                GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, blipHandle);
                                float dist = World.GetDistance(playerPos, blipPos);
                                allBlips.Add(new Tuple<int, string, int, float>(blipHandle, blipTypeNames[i], missionBlipTypes[i], dist));
                                blipHandle = Function.Call<int>(Hash.GET_NEXT_BLIP_INFO_ID, missionBlipTypes[i]);
                            }
                        }

                        allBlips.Sort((a, b) => a.Item4.CompareTo(b.Item4));

                        foreach (var blip in allBlips)
                        {
                            availableBlipHandles.Add(blip.Item1);
                            availableBlipNames.Add(blip.Item2);
                            availableBlipTypes.Add(blip.Item3);
                        }
                    }

                    if (availableBlipHandles.Count == 0)
                    {
                        Speech.Info("No markers found");
                    }
                    else
                    {
                        // Cycle BACKWARDS
                        blipCycleIndex--;
                        if (blipCycleIndex < 0)
                            blipCycleIndex = availableBlipHandles.Count - 1;

                        int selectedHandle = availableBlipHandles[blipCycleIndex];
                        string selectedName = availableBlipNames[blipCycleIndex];
                        int selectedType = availableBlipTypes[blipCycleIndex];

                        if (!Function.Call<bool>(Hash.DOES_BLIP_EXIST, selectedHandle))
                        {
                            lastBlipScanTicks = 0;
                            Speech.Info("Marker no longer available, rescanning");
                        }
                        else
                        {
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 blipPos = Function.Call<GTA.Math.Vector3>(Hash.GET_BLIP_INFO_ID_COORD, selectedHandle);
                            GTA.Math.Vector3 playerPos = Game.Player.Character.Position;

                            float dx = blipPos.X - playerPos.X;
                            float dy = blipPos.Y - playerPos.Y;
                            float distance = (float)Math.Sqrt(dx * dx + dy * dy);
                            // iter-37 N12: -dx converts the clockwise atan2 bearing to the
                            // counterclockwise (GTA-heading) convention getDir expects —
                            // east/west were mirrored in every spoken blip direction.
                            double angle = Math.Atan2(-dx, dy) * (180.0 / Math.PI);
                            if (angle < 0) angle += 360;

                            string direction = getDir((float)angle);

                            Function.Call(Hash.SET_NEW_WAYPOINT, blipPos.X, blipPos.Y);

                            trackedBlipHandle = selectedHandle;
                            trackedBlipType = selectedType;
                            missionTrackingActive = true;
                            waypointTrackingActive = true;
                            missionBeepTicks = 0;
                            waypointBeepTicks = 0;

                            string announcement = "Marker " + (blipCycleIndex + 1) + " of " + availableBlipHandles.Count +
                                ". " + selectedName + ", " + (int)distance + " meters " + direction + ". Waypoint set.";
                            Speech.Info(announcement);
                        }
                    }
                }

                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.NumPad6 && !keyState[6])
                {
                    keyState[6] = true; // was the lone handler without the repeat guard: holding the key re-ran the full ped scan on every OS auto-repeat
                    float detectRadius = GetDetectionRadius();
                    Ped[] peds = World.GetNearbyPeds(Game.Player.Character.Position, detectRadius);
                    string status = "";
                    List<Result> results = new List<Result>();
                    bool valid = false;

                    foreach (Ped ped in peds)
                    {
                        valid = false;
                        if (getSetting("onscreen") == 0 && hashes.ContainsKey(ped.Model.NativeValue.ToString()) && ped.IsVisible && !ped.IsDead)
                            valid = true;

                        if (getSetting("onscreen") == 1 && hashes.ContainsKey(ped.Model.NativeValue.ToString()) && ped.IsVisible && ped.IsOnScreen && !ped.IsDead)
                            valid = true;
                        if (valid)
                        {
                            if (hashes[ped.Model.NativeValue.ToString()] != "player_one" && hashes[ped.Model.NativeValue.ToString()] != "player_two" && hashes[ped.Model.NativeValue.ToString()] != "player_zero")
                            {
                                string name = (status + " " + hashes[ped.Model.NativeValue.ToString()]);
                                double xyDistance = Math.Round(World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, ped.Position) - Math.Abs(Game.Player.Character.Position.Z - ped.Position.Z), 1);
                                double zDistance = Math.Round(ped.Position.Z - Game.Player.Character.Position.Z, 1);
                                string direction = getDir(calculate_x_y_angle(Game.Player.Character.Position.X, Game.Player.Character.Position.Y, ped.Position.X, ped.Position.Y, 0));
                                Result result = new Result(name, xyDistance, zDistance, direction);
                                results.Add(result);
                            }
                        }
                    }

                    Speech.Ambient(listToString(results, "Nearest Characters: "));

                }

                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.NumPad5 && !keyState[5])
                {
                    keyState[5] = true;
                    float detectRadius = GetDetectionRadius();
                    Prop[] props = World.GetNearbyProps(Game.Player.Character.Position, detectRadius);
                    string status = "";
                    List<Result> results = new List<Result>();

                    bool valid = false;

                    foreach (Prop prop in props)
                    {
                        valid = false;

                        if (getSetting("onscreen") == 0 && hashes.ContainsKey(prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()) && prop.IsVisible && !prop.IsAttachedTo(Game.Player.Character) && (hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].Contains("door") || hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].Contains("gate")))
                            valid = true;

                        if (getSetting("onscreen") == 1 && hashes.ContainsKey(prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()) && prop.IsVisible && prop.IsOnScreen && !prop.IsAttachedTo(Game.Player.Character) && (hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].Contains("door") || hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].Contains("gate")))
                            valid = true;

                        if (valid)
                        {
                            string name = (status + " " + hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()]);
                            double xyDistance = Math.Round(World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, prop.Position) - Math.Abs(Game.Player.Character.Position.Z - prop.Position.Z), 1);
                            double zDistance = Math.Round(prop.Position.Z - Game.Player.Character.Position.Z, 1);
                            string direction = getDir(calculate_x_y_angle(Game.Player.Character.Position.X, Game.Player.Character.Position.Y, prop.Position.X, prop.Position.Y, 0));
                            Result result = new Result(name, xyDistance, zDistance, direction);
                            results.Add(result);

                        }
                    }

                    Speech.Ambient(listToString(results, "Nearest Doors: "));
                }

                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.NumPad8 && !keyState[8])
                {
                    keyState[8] = true;
                    float detectRadius = GetDetectionRadius();
                    Prop[] props = World.GetNearbyProps(Game.Player.Character.Position, detectRadius);
                    string status = "";
                    List<Result> results = new List<Result>();
                    bool valid = false;

                    foreach (Prop prop in props)
                    {
                        valid = false;

                        if (getSetting("onscreen") == 0 && hashes.ContainsKey(prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()) && prop.IsVisible && !prop.IsAttachedTo(Game.Player.Character) && !hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].Contains("door") && !hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].Contains("gate"))
                            valid = true;

                        if (getSetting("onscreen") == 1 && hashes.ContainsKey(prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()) && prop.IsVisible && prop.IsOnScreen && !prop.IsAttachedTo(Game.Player.Character) && !hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].Contains("door") && !hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()].Contains("gate"))
                            valid = true;

                        if (valid)
                        {
                            // iter-52: hashes.txt gives the raw model name, so a vending
                            // machine reads as "prop vend soda 01". Append what the object
                            // is actually FOR when the catalogue knows it.
                            string name = (status + " " + hashes[prop.Model.NativeValue.ToString()])
                                + InteractionSuffix(unchecked((int)prop.Model.NativeValue));
                            double xyDistance = Math.Round(World.GetDistance(Game.Player.Character.Position, prop.Position) - Math.Abs(Game.Player.Character.Position.Z - prop.Position.Z), 1);
                            double zDistance = Math.Round(prop.Position.Z - Game.Player.Character.Position.Z, 1);
                            string direction = getDir(calculate_x_y_angle(Game.Player.Character.Position.X, Game.Player.Character.Position.Y, prop.Position.X, prop.Position.Y, 0));
                            Result result = new Result(name, xyDistance, zDistance, direction);
                            results.Add(result);

                        }
                    }

                    Speech.Ambient(listToString(results, "Nearest Objects: "));

                }

                if (e.KeyCode == Keys.NumPad0 && !keyState[0])
                {
                    keyState[0] = true;
